\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For January 31\b0\par\par\uc2 2,157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2012\par 08:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 4.0% IN DEC, BEATS FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production rose 4.0% in December from the previous month, the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday, as the impact of the flooding in Thailand on Japanese manufacturers began to ease. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: TO TAKE DECISIVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister issued a fresh warning Tuesday that he will take "decisive steps" if speculators push the yen up too sharply, after the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to its strongest level in around three months overnight. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER AZUMI: WANT CHINA TO "INTERNATIONALIZE" YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Chinese side holds Japanese government bonds, and for our part, we have decided to buy yuan-denominated Chinese government debt because we really want China to internationalize the yuan, we find it advantageous for Japan to hold such debt, and we like to strengthen our economic relationships" with Beijing, Jun Azumi said during a parliamentary session. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SCHIFF: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD ONLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF HIGH VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during periods of high volatility, a senior official at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday, adding that such action has little lasting effect. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SAYS ASIA HAS ROOM FOR STIMULUS IF OUTLOOK DARKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia has so far proved resilient to the European sovereign-debt crisis and slowing global growth, and countries in the region have room to take growth-boosting steps in case of a sharp downturn, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AMRO HEAD WEI: ASIA REMAINS AT RISK FROM EURO-ZONE SHOCKS IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies remain at risk from shocks coming from Europe's debt crisis in 2012, said Wei Benhua, the director of a new Asian research office and a former deputy of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bureau. (published 0306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S KOREA SAYS TO TAME INFLATION EVEN AT EXPENSE OF GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean President Lee Myung-bak Tuesday said the government must anchor inflation even at the expense of weaker growth, placing price stability firmly at the top of the administration's economic priorities even as December's industrial output unexpectedly contracted. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA CUTS LAST FISCAL YEAR GDP GROWTH ESTIMATE TO 8.4% FROM 8.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government Tuesday lowered slightly its estimate of the country's growth in gross domestic product for the last fiscal year ended March 31, 2011, to 8.4% from 8.5%. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA END-SEPTEMBER EXTERNAL FINANCIAL ASSETS TOTALED $4.67 TRILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's total foreign assets came to $4.665 trillion at the end of September, up around 1% from the end of June, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said Tuesday. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO EXPORTS -2.1% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's exports of cars, trucks and buses declined 2.1% on year in December, falling for the first time in five months, as Japanese car makers sought to cut back exports from their home country amid the strong yen. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO PRODUCTION +13.4% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Production of cars, trucks and buses in Japan increased 13.4% on year in December, rising for the third consecutive month, as car makers revved up output with their normalized parts supply chains to make up for lost production after the March earthquake. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA DEC CAPITAL CITY HOUSE PRICES DOWN 0.2% -RP DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian monthly house prices declined once again in December, adding to growing concern among banks and property firms that a deterioration in prices across the country will resume this year. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS CHIEF: ASIAN ECONOMIES NEED IMF TO REMAIN ACTIVE IN REGION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies need the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  to continue playing an active role in the region and to complement regional financial arrangements, the chief of Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PBOC DOESN'T HOLD TUESDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't conduct its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, in a move apparently aimed at easing tight liquidity conditions in the banking system as a large amount of reverse repurchase agreements will mature this week, traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES SETS COUPON FOR 20-YEAR TREASURY BOND AT 5.875% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines fixed at an auction Tuesday the coupon for a 20-year treasury bond at 5.875%. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAH SING BANK TO ISSUE AROUND S$200 MLN OF BONDS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to issue around S$200 million worth of subordinated bonds, a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday showed. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WHARF PRICES US$600M BOND AT 99.515 TO YIELD 4.735%, TSYS +400BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wharf Ltd. has priced a US$600 million five-year dollar bond at 99.515 to yield 4.735%, or 400 basis points over the yield on the 0.875% January 2017 U.S. Treasury, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUTCHISON WHAMPOA PLANS TAP OF 2017, 2022 DOLLAR BONDS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Whampoa Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to price today a tap worth up to US$1 billion of the five- and 10-year dollar bonds that it sold earlier this month, according to a term sheet for the planned deal seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA JANUARY MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY LIKELY SLOWED - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's manufacturing activity likely contracted in January after a brief rebound in December, as factories and plants sat idle across the country during the just ended weeklong Lunar New Year holiday, economists said. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ANGANG STEEL ESTIMATES LOSS FOR 2011; SHARES TUMBLE ON PROFIT WARNING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Profit warnings from Angang Steel Co. and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Maanshan Iron & Steel Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . sent shares of the two Chinese steel makers plunging Tuesday, as investors fretted that a softening property market as well as higher raw material costs would continue to weigh on their profitability. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA COMMUNICATIONS CONSTRUCTION SLASHES SHANGHAI IPO SIZE TO $794 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Port machinery manufacturer \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Communications Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Tuesday cut the size of its planned Shanghai initial public offering to CNY5 billion from CNY20 billion, in the latest indication of weak investor appetite and highlighting that the IPO market this year is off to a slow start. (published 0402 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: DAIICHI SANKYO LOGS 3Q LOSS, CUTS VIEW ON RANBAXY WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daiichi Sankyo Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it fell into the red for the fiscal third quarter and further lowered its full-year outlook, hurt again by the stubbornly strong yen and legal costs associated with its Indian unit. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAIWA SECURITIES OCT-DEC GROUP NET LOSS Y21.6B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daiwa Securities Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported its fourth consecutive quarterly loss in the October-December period due to higher operating expenses and lower commissions from investment banking amid sluggish business in equity finance. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HONDA 3Q NET PROFIT SINKS 41% ON YEN, THAI FLOODS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that its net profit dropped 41% in the fiscal third quarter, as the strong yen cut into its overseas earnings and flooding in Thailand caused a setback in its production recovery after the earthquake in Japan. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAIC MOTOR: EXPECT 2011 NET PROFIT UP MORE THAN 40% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAIC Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., China's largest car maker by sales, said Tuesday it expects its net profit for 2011 to have risen more than 40% from the prior year due to higher car sales and an acquisition of its parent's assets. (published 2338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MOODY'S CUTS QANTAS CREDIT RATING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Tuesday had its credit rating downgraded by Moody's Investors Service partly on the impact of higher fuel prices, but the airline managed to retain investment-grade status thanks to its strong domestic flights unit. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KOREAN AIR\f28 \uc2 \f2  SWINGS TO CONSOLIDATED 2011 NET LOSS ON HIGH FUEL COSTS, WEAK WON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Flag carrier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korean Air Lines Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it swung to a consolidated net loss last year because of a surge in jet fuel expenses, a weaker local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and sluggish cargo demand amid economic uncertainties around the globe, though its fourth-quarter net profit jumped due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIR NEW ZEALAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  CEO ROB FYFE TO STEP DOWN DEC 31 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rob Fyfe\f28 \uc2 \f2  will step down at the end of his term Dec. 31, the Auckland-based airline said in a statement Tuesday. (published 0134 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CEBU AIR EXPECTS PROFITABILITY IN 2012 DESPITE FUEL PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cebu Air Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Philippines largest budget carrier by fleet and revenue, said Tuesday it expects to be profitable this year in spite of expensive fuel. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KIRIN HOLDINGS CUTS LAST FY NET PFT VIEW ON ASSET WRITE-DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kirin Holdings Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that it sharply revised downward its net profit outlook for the business year ended December, saddled with a write-down of fixed assets and a securities valuation loss. (published 0245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WOOLWORTHS TO DIVEST DICK SMITH ELECTRONICS BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian retail giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woolworths Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to divest its Dick Smith electronics business following a strategic review. (published 2320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STATE BANK OF INDIA EXECUTIVE: MAY ISSUE SHARES AT INR1,800-INR2,000 TO GOVT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 31-01-12 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank Of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  may issue shares to the government at INR1,800-INR2,000 apiece in a preferential allotment aimed at injecting up to INR79 billion into the lender. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HYUNDAI MOBIS\f28 \uc2 \f2  GETS AUTO-PARTS ORDERS FROM GM, CHRYSLER WORTH $1.07 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Mobis Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's largest auto parts maker by sales, said Tuesday it has signed contracts worth a total of $1.07 billion to supply core auto parts to \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Motors Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and Chrysler Group LLC. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BANK OF CHINA, BOCOM TO SPEND US$92.3 MLN FOR FIRST TAIWAN BRANCHES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan government has agreed two major Chinese banks can spend a combined US$92.3 million establishing their first branches on the island, the latest move by the two sides to mutually open up their financial sectors. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP ON GREEK HOPES; TOKYO EXPORTERS UNDERPERFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian stock markets were modestly higher Tuesday after encouraging comments from the Greek prime minister on ongoing debt talks, the euro-zone's move toward a closer fiscal union and positive economic data in Japan, but earnings concerns weighed Tokyo exporters and China steelmakers. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN, US TO MEET THURSDAY TO DISCUSS IRAN SANCTIONS -JAPAN MOFA OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan will have its second meeting with the U.S. on Thursday to discuss applying sanctions against Iran over its suspected nuclear weapons development program, a Japan foreign ministry official said Tuesday. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN EDANO: NOT CONSIDERING SEPARATING OVERSIGHT OF ENERGY INDUSTRY FROM METI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's trade and industry minister Yukio Edano said Tuesday he isn't thinking about separating oversight of the energy industry from his own ministry, denying a local media report that he is considering setting up an independent regulator. (published 0027 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: IAEA CALLS FOR TOUGHER ANTI-DISASTER PLAN AT JAPAN NUCLEAR PLANTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Atomic Energy Agency Tuesday called for a more comprehensive disaster management plan at Japanese nuclear plants, as regulators struggle to regain the public's trust in its ability to keep reactors operating safely after the Fukushima nuclear disaster in March. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S PORT KEMBLA COAL TERMINAL FACES STRIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Workers at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . managed Port Kembla Coal Terminal in eastern Australia will launch a seven-day strike from Wednesday after negotiations failed to resolve a labor dispute, the Construction, Forestry, Mining and Energy Union said. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: TOKYO PLANS OWN 1-GW GAS-POWER PLANT FOR BASIC PUBLIC SERVICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's capital city government is planning to generate its own electricity to cover basic public services in an effort to avoid the recurrence of rolling blackouts that were implemented in the aftermath of the March 2011 earthquake and tsunami. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  CFO: LOOKING FOR GAS ASSETS IN WESTERN CANADA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is looking to buy natural gas assets in Western Canada, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ryoichi Ueda\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Japanese trading company's chief financial officer, said Tuesday. (published 0551 GMT) [ 31-01-12 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120131e81v000n7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
