\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,000 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2012\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 4.0% IN DEC, BEATS FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production rose 4.0% in December from the previous month, the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday, as the impact of the flooding in Thailand on Japanese manufacturers began to ease. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: TO TAKE DECISIVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister issued a fresh warning Tuesday that he will take "decisive steps" if speculators push the yen up too sharply, after the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to its strongest level in around three months overnight. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER AZUMI: WANT CHINA TO "INTERNATIONALIZE" YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Chinese side holds Japanese government bonds, and for our part, we have decided to buy yuan-denominated Chinese government debt because we really want China to internationalize the yuan, we find it advantageous for Japan to hold such debt, and we like to strengthen our economic relationships" with Beijing, Jun Azumi said during a parliamentary session. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SCHIFF: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD ONLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF HIGH VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during periods of high volatility, a senior official at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday, adding that such action has little lasting effect. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SAYS ASIA HAS ROOM FOR STIMULUS IF OUTLOOK DARKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia has so far proved resilient to the European sovereign-debt crisis and slowing global growth, and countries in the region have room to take growth-boosting steps in case of a sharp downturn, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AMRO HEAD WEI: ASIA REMAINS AT RISK FROM EURO-ZONE SHOCKS IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies remain at risk from shocks coming from Europe's debt crisis in 2012, said Wei Benhua, the director of a new Asian research office and a former deputy of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bureau. (published 0306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S KOREA SAYS TO TAME INFLATION EVEN AT EXPENSE OF GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean President Lee Myung-bak Tuesday said the government must anchor inflation even at the expense of weaker growth, placing price stability firmly at the top of the administration's economic priorities even as December's industrial output unexpectedly contracted. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA CUTS LAST FISCAL YEAR GDP GROWTH ESTIMATE TO 8.4% FROM 8.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government Tuesday lowered slightly its estimate of the country's growth in gross domestic product for the last fiscal year ended March 31, 2011, to 8.4% from 8.5%. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA END-SEPTEMBER EXTERNAL FINANCIAL ASSETS TOTALED $4.67 TRILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's total foreign assets came to $4.665 trillion at the end of September, up around 1% from the end of June, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said Tuesday. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO EXPORTS -2.1% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's exports of cars, trucks and buses declined 2.1% on year in December, falling for the first time in five months, as Japanese car makers sought to cut back exports from their home country amid the strong yen. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO PRODUCTION +13.4% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Production of cars, trucks and buses in Japan increased 13.4% on year in December, rising for the third consecutive month, as car makers revved up output with their normalized parts supply chains to make up for lost production after the March earthquake. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA DEC CAPITAL CITY HOUSE PRICES DOWN 0.2% -RP DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian monthly house prices declined once again in December, adding to growing concern among banks and property firms that a deterioration in prices across the country will resume this year. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS CHIEF: ASIAN ECONOMIES NEED IMF TO REMAIN ACTIVE IN REGION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies need the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  to continue playing an active role in the region and to complement regional financial arrangements, the chief of Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC DOESN'T HOLD TUESDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't conduct its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, in a move apparently aimed at easing tight liquidity conditions in the banking system as a large amount of reverse repurchase agreements will mature this week, traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES SETS COUPON FOR 20-YEAR TREASURY BOND AT 5.875% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines fixed at an auction Tuesday the coupon for a 20-year treasury bond at 5.875%. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DAH SING BANK TO ISSUE AROUND S$200 MLN OF BONDS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to issue around S$200 million worth of subordinated bonds, a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday showed. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WHARF PRICES US$600M BOND AT 99.515 TO YIELD 4.735%, TSYS +400BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wharf Ltd. has priced a US$600 million five-year dollar bond at 99.515 to yield 4.735%, or 400 basis points over the yield on the 0.875% January 2017 U.S. Treasury, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HUTCHISON WHAMPOA PLANS TAP OF 2017, 2022 DOLLAR BONDS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Whampoa Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to price today a tap worth up to US$1 billion of the five- and 10-year dollar bonds that it sold earlier this month, according to a term sheet for the planned deal seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 0658 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA JANUARY MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY LIKELY SLOWED - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's manufacturing activity likely contracted in January after a brief rebound in December, as factories and plants sat idle across the country during the just ended weeklong Lunar New Year holiday, economists said. (published 0126 GMT) [ 31-01-12 0702GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120131e81v000ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
