\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 863 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2012\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 4.0% IN DEC, BEATS FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production rose 4.0% in December from the previous month, the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday, as the impact of the flooding in Thailand on Japanese manufacturers began to ease. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: TO TAKE DECISIVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister issued a fresh warning Tuesday that he will take "decisive steps" if speculators push the yen up too sharply, after the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to its strongest level in around three months overnight. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SCHIFF: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD ONLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF HIGH VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during periods of high volatility, a senior official at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday, adding that such action has little lasting effect. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF SAYS ASIA HAS ROOM FOR STIMULUS IF OUTLOOK DARKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia has so far proved resilient to the European sovereign-debt crisis and slowing global growth, and countries in the region have room to take growth-boosting steps in case of a sharp downturn, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AMRO HEAD WEI: ASIA REMAINS AT RISK FROM EURO-ZONE SHOCKS IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies remain at risk from shocks coming from Europe's debt crisis in 2012, said Wei Benhua, the director of a new Asian research office and a former deputy of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bureau. (published 0306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA PRESIDENT: MUST ANCHOR INFLATION EVEN IF GROWTH WEAKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean President Lee Myung-bak Tuesday said the government must anchor inflation even if growth suffers slightly, re-asserting the administration's policy priority for the year even as downside risks to the economy grow. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UNEXPECTEDLY CONTRACTS IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial output in South Korea unexpectedly contracted in December, government data showed Tuesday, underscoring slowing economic momentum as the ongoing euro zone sovereign debt crisis muffles domestic and external demand. (published 0055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA CUTS LAST FISCAL YEAR GDP GROWTH ESTIMATE TO 8.4% FROM 8.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian government Tuesday lowered slightly its estimate of the country's growth in gross domestic product for the last fiscal year ended March 31, 2011, to 8.4% from 8.5%. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO EXPORTS -2.1% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's exports of cars, trucks and buses declined 2.1% on year in December, falling for the first time in five months, as Japanese car makers sought to cut back exports from their home country amid the strong yen. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO PRODUCTION +13.4% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Production of cars, trucks and buses in Japan increased 13.4% on year in December, rising for the third consecutive month, as car makers revved up output with their normalized parts supply chains to make up for lost production after the March earthquake. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA DEC CAPITAL CITY HOUSE PRICES DOWN 0.2% -RP DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian monthly house prices declined once again in December, adding to growing concern among banks and property firms that a deterioration in prices across the country will resume this year. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PM BRIEFED BY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ON ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard received a briefing on the economic outlook Tuesday from the chief of the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and met with the head of the Australian Securities Exchange. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS CHIEF: ASIAN ECONOMIES NEED IMF TO REMAIN ACTIVE IN REGION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies need the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  to continue playing an active role in the region and to complement regional financial arrangements, the chief of Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC DOESN'T HOLD TUESDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't conduc