\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 911 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2012\par 04:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 4.0% IN DEC, BEATS FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production rose 4.0% in December from the previous month, the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday, as the impact of the flooding in Thailand on Japanese manufacturers began to ease. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: TO TAKE DECISIVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister issued a fresh warning Tuesday that he will take "decisive steps" if speculators push the yen up too sharply, after the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to its strongest level in around three months overnight. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF SCHIFF: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD ONLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF HIGH VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during periods of high volatility, a senior official at the International Monetary Fund said Tuesday, adding that such action has little lasting effect. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UNEXPECTEDLY CONTRACTS IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial output in South Korea unexpectedly contracted in December, government data showed Tuesday, underscoring slowing economic momentum as the ongoing euro zone sovereign debt crisis muffles domestic and external demand. (published 0055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: CHINA, INDIA HAVE ROOM FOR FISCAL STIMULUS, BOJ COULD EASE MORE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia has so far proved resilient to the European sovereign-debt crisis and slowing global growth, and countries in the region have room to take growth-boosting steps in case of a sharp downturn, the International Monetary Fund said. (published 0038 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: UPDATE: EU GOVERNMENTS CLOSER TO FISCAL UNION DEAL, EUR500B BAILOUT FUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaders of 25 European Union governments agreed Monday night on what some were billing as a historic pact to move to closer fiscal union and to finally sign off on the details of a EUR500 billion permanent bailout fund for the euro zone that should come into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at mid-year. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA DEC CAPITAL CITY HOUSE PRICES DOWN 0.2% -RP DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian monthly house prices declined once again in December, adding to growing concern among banks and property firms that a deterioration in prices across the country will resume this year. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA DECEMBER BUSINESS CONFIDENCE INDEX RISES -NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business confidence picked up a touch in December, likely boosted by rate cuts from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the broader mood among executives remains subdued, according to a closely watched monthly survey. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN PRIVATE-SECTOR CREDIT +0.3% IN DEC VS NOV \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit to the Australian private sector rose a seasonally adjusted 0.3% in December from November and rose 3.5% from a year earlier, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PM BRIEFED BY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ON ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard received a briefing on the economic outlook Tuesday from the chief of the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and met with the head of the Australian Securities Exchange. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS CHIEF: ASIAN ECONOMIES NEED IMF TO REMAIN ACTIVE IN REGION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies need the International Monetary Fund to continue playing an active role in the region and to complement regional financial arrangements, the chief of Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE DECEMBER M1 MONEY SUPPLY S$129.12 BLN VS S$130.77 BLN NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 M1 is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in active circulation and demand deposits. (published 0205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE 4Q UNEMPLOYMENT RATE 2.0%, UNCHANGED FROM 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's unemployment rate was unchanged in the fourth quarter compared with the previous three months, as more jobs were created while the number of redundancies also increased. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC DOESN'T HOLD TUESDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't conduct its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, in a move apparently aimed at easing tight liquidity conditions in the banking system as a large amount of reverse repurchase agreements will mature this week, traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMANY'S LANXESS PLANS TO ISSUE OFFSHORE YUAN-DENOMINATED BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German chemical company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lanxess AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to issue an offshore yuan-denominated bond, a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JOHNSON MATTHEY PLANS TO ISSUE OFFSHORE YUAN-DENOMINATED BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Johnson Matthey PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's largest supplier of catalytic converters, plans to issue an offshore yuan-denominated bond, a person familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SHANDONG HI-SPEED GROUP TO SELL CNY2 BLN 10-YEAR BONDS SOON - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toll road operator Shandong HI-Speed Group Co. plans to sell CNY2 billion of 10-year bonds on the domestic market soon, a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WHARF PRICES US$600M BOND AT 99.515 TO YIELD 4.735%, TSYS +400BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wharf Ltd. has priced a US$600 million five-year dollar bond at 99.515 to yield 4.735%, or 400 basis points over the yield on the 0.875% January 2017 U.S. Treasury, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par CHINA JANUARY MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY LIKELY SLOWED - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's manufacturing activity likely contracted in January after a brief rebound in December, as factories and plants sat idle across the country during the just ended weeklong Lunar New Year holiday, economists said. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 31-01-12 0302GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120131e81v00060\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
