\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2012\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN TRADE MIN EDANO: VERY DIFFICULT TO GET THROUGH SUMMER WITHOUT ANY NUCLEAR REACTOR RESTARTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese trade and industry minister Yukio Edano said Thursday that the government is exploring contingency plans to deal with potential power shortages in the summer due to the unavailability of nuclear power. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: NEW CHIEF OF S&P DEFENDS MOVES IN FIRST INTERVIEW SINCE TAKING JOB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Doug Peterson, the new president of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services, defended the firm's downgrades of U.S. and European sovereign bonds, rebuffing criticism the ratings company had become more aggressive following the financial crisis. (published 0025 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB NOWOTNY DISCOURAGES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SUPPORT EURO -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing board member Ewald Nowotny said in an interview with the Nikkei that the euro was moving in a "normal range," and the yen's rise against the European unit wasn't one-sided--a comment the Nikkei characterized as a warning against potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's authorities to curb the yen against the euro. (published 2324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SURPRISE NZ 4Q INFLATION FALL GIVES RBNZ MORE ROOM TO REMAIN ON HOLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The first quarterly fall in New Zealand's consumer price index in two years adds to the likelihood that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand will keep its benchmark interest rate at its current low level for some time to come, economists said. (published 0258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN DECEMBER UNEMPLOYMENT RATE UNCHANGED AT 5.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy lost 29,300 workers in December as several sectors faced pressure from a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and growing economic concerns around the globe, though a steady unemployment rate at 5.2% indicated still firm prospects for the mining-driven economy. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN RBA SOLD A$737M IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold a net A$737 million in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in December, figures issued by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday show. (published 0036 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PREMIER: CAN STUDY QATAR PROPOSAL ON USING OWN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOR TRADE SETTLEMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said China can study a proposal by Qatar on using the two countries' own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for bilateral trade settlements, the official Xinhua News Agency reported Thursday. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF BOARD APPROVES TALKS ON EXPANDED GREEK LOANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund executive board Wednesday gave approval for staff to start official negotiations with Greece for an expanded loan program, a spokeswoman said. (published 2225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  OFFERS CNY183 BLN REVERSE REPOS; LIQUIDITY SQUEEZE EASES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday offered CNY183 billion of 14-day reverse repurchase agreements at its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , marking its latest efforts to ease a temporary liquidity squeeze in the banking system following a CNY169 billion similar offering on Tuesday. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: BRAZIL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CUTS BENCHMARK INTEREST RATE TO 10.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday lowered, as expected, its benchmark interest rate and hinted it may continue to cut rates ahead amid concern about the impact of global economic problems on the domestic economy. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RIZAL COMMERCIAL BANKING PRICED US$200 MLN BOND AT PAR TO YIELD 5.25% - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rizal Commercial Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has priced a five-year $200 million U.S. dollar-denominated bond at par to yield 5.25%, a term sheet for the deal seen by Dow Jones Newswires Thursday showed. (published 0057 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par FED WATCH: ST. LOUIS FED SAYS CBO DOESN'T FORECAST DEFICITS WELL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Congress's long history of underestimating future budget deficits suggests the current outlook for the nation's finances may be even grimmer than many now expect. (published 2046 GMT) [ 19-01-12 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120119e81j0005g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\