\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2012\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN PREPARED TO SUPPORT EUROPE, INCLUDING LENDING TO IMF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior Japanese government official said Thursday that Japan stands ready to back efforts by European countries to address its financial crisis, including by lending to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OMAN CTRL BK HEAD: IMF HAS ASKED GCC STATES TO BOOST CONTRIBUTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The oil-rich Gulf Cooperation Council, or GCC, states have been approached by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  to increase their financial contributions as the fund seeks to boost its resource base by an extra $500 billion to $600 billion to help battle the euro-zone debt crisis, Oman's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said Thursday. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN METI MIN EDANO: JAPAN MAY HAVE NO REACTORS ONLINE IN SUMMER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese trade and industry minister Yukio Edano said Thursday that Japan may have no nuclear reactors operating during the peak power demand season in summer, a worrying scenario that could hit domestic production and accelerate the exodus of businesses from the nation. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: NEW CHIEF OF S&P DEFENDS MOVES IN FIRST INTERVIEW SINCE TAKING JOB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Doug Peterson, the new president of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services, defended the firm's downgrades of U.S. and European sovereign bonds, rebuffing criticism the ratings company had become more aggressive following the financial crisis. (published 0025 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB NOWOTNY DISCOURAGES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SUPPORT EURO -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing board member Ewald Nowotny said in an interview with the Nikkei that the euro was moving in a "normal range," and the yen's rise against the European unit wasn't one-sided--a comment the Nikkei characterized as a warning against potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's authorities to curb the yen against the euro. (published 2324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SURPRISE NZ 4Q INFLATION FALL GIVES RBNZ MORE ROOM TO REMAIN ON HOLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The first quarterly fall in New Zealand's consumer price index in two years adds to the likelihood that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand will keep its benchmark interest rate at its current low level for some time to come, economists said. (published 0258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN DECEMBER UNEMPLOYMENT RATE UNCHANGED AT 5.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy lost 29,300 workers in December as several sectors faced pressure from a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and growing economic concerns around the globe, though a steady unemployment rate at 5.2% indicated still firm prospects for the mining-driven economy. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA 2011 FDI UP 20.2% ON YEAR AT IDR175.3 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Actual foreign direct investment in Indonesia grew 20.2% last year to IDR175.3 trillion, the official Investment Coordinating Board said Thursday. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN RBA SOLD A$737M IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold a net A$737 million in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in December, figures issued by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday show. (published 0036 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PREMIER: CAN STUDY QATAR PROPOSAL ON USING OWN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOR TRADE SETTLEMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said China can study a proposal by Qatar on using the two countries' own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for bilateral trade settlements, the official Xinhua News Agency reported Thursday. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF BOARD APPROVES TALKS ON EXPANDED GREEK LOANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive board Wednesday gave approval for staff to start official negotiations with Greece for an expanded loan program, a spokeswoman said. (published 2225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  OFFERS CNY183 BLN REVERSE REPOS; LIQUIDITY SQUEEZE EASES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday offered CNY183 billion of 14-day reverse repurchase agreements at its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , marking its latest efforts to ease a temporary liquidity squeeze in the banking system following a CNY169 billion similar offering on Tuesday. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI DEPUTY PM: DECEMBER EXPORTS LIKELY SHRANK 2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Deputy Prime Minister Kittiratt Na-Ranong said Thursday exports in 