\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan finmin: trust in EFSF bonds not shaken by downgrade\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2012\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Japan still trusts euro bailout bonds after S&P cut-finmin\par \par \uc2 * Azumi says EFSF bonds remain attractive\par \par \uc2 * Watching \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves when asked about euro/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Azumi\par \par \uc2 * Azumi reiterates \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep cutting Iran oil imports\par \par \uc2 * Japan, U.S. to start discussing Iran sanctions on Wed\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background, detail)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 17 (Reuters) - Japan's trust in bonds issued by the euro zone's rescue fund has not been shaken by \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgrade of the European Financial Stability Facility's credit rating, Finance Minister Jun Azumi said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Azumi also said there was no change in his view that Japan would continue to cut Iranian oil imports following a U.S. push to prevent Iran from making nuclear weapons even after the premier dismissed his view as "personal opinion".\par \par \uc2 The U.S. rating agency cut its top AAA credit rating of the euro zone's rescue fund by one notch to AA+ on Monday, three days after it cut the ratings of France and Austria by the same margin and downgraded seven other euro zone nations.\par \par \uc2 But Azumi said the EFSF bonds remained "attractive" investment for Japan.\par \par \uc2 "Japan has bought them by certain amounts and our stance will not immediately change just because of the downgrade," Azumi told reporters after a cabinet meeting.\par \par \uc2 Japan has so far bought 3.535 billion euros worth of EFSF bonds of a total 21 billion euros worth of such bonds sold by the Luxembourg-based fund, set up in May 2010.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have said they would continue to buy EFSF bonds by tapping euro assets in its foreign reserves providing that Europe makes efforts to resolve the region's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The euro hovered barely above a 17-month trough against the dollar and an 11-year low against the yen on Tuesday after S&P downgrading of Europe's bailout fund dealt the euro zone yet another blow.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to respond to the weakening euro, Azumi said he wanted to carefully examine current movements in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.\par \par \uc2 Azumi, who vowed last week to cut Iranian oil imports in response to U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner's appeal for support of U.S. sanctions against Tehran, said such reduction was in keeping with Tokyo's longer-term effort.\par \par \uc2 "Japan has cut Iranian oil imports by nearly 40 percent (over the past five years) by making efforts to prevent it from affecting the economy," Azumi said. "I understand that we're in a direction towards further reduction as well. This is the stance that I have expressed."\par \par \uc2 He said Japan and the United States will kickoff bilateral negotiations at working levels to discuss U.S. sanctions on Iran from Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Azumi was expressing his personal opinion and that Tokyo had yet to decide how to respond to Washington's sanctions.\par \par \uc2 A new U.S. law signed by President Barack Obama on New Year's Eve would freeze out of the U.S. financial system any institution dealing with Iran's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which processes its oil revenues.\par \par \uc2 If fully applied, the law would make it impossible for most countries to buy Iranian oil. Washington is offering waivers to countries to let them keep buying Iranian oil for now, but demanding they gradually cut their imports back.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/AZUMI  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120120e81h0003y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
