\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan Dec monetary base rises 13.5 pct yr/yr\b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2012\par 01:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Banknote circulation hits record high in Dec\par \par \uc2  * Households, corporations continue to hoard cash after quake \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail)\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Japan's monetary base rose 13.5 percent in December from a year earlier, \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  data showed on Thursday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to supply funds to secure liquidity in the banking system.\par \par \uc2  The balance of banknotes in circulation rose 2.3 percent to a record high of 81.572 trillion yen ($1.06 trillion) as households and corporations continued to hoard cash following the devastating March earthquake and tsunami, according to the BOJ.\par \par \uc2  Japan's monetary base fell 43.3 percent in December on a seasonally adjusted basis from the month before, after a 41.2 percent gain in November, due to the settlement of money from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 31. \par \par \uc2   ($1 = 76.7400 Japanese yen) \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kaori Kaneko; Editing by Joseph Radford)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/MONETARYBASE (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120105e8150000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
