\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Hits 3-Week Low Vs Yen On Exporters' Selling\b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2011\par 06:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Dollar hits three-week low against yen on selling by exporters\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry to release December \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data; traders expect the figure to be zero\par \par \uc2 -- Euro also lower against yen, fall below Y100.00 likely soon\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar fell to a three-week low against the yen Friday in Asia due to last-minute settlement orders by Japanese exporters that also pushed down the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback fell to as low as Y77.51 during the Asian session, the lowest level since Dec. 9. At 0450 GMT. It was at Y77.53 from Y77.62 in New York Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the impact of small dollar-selling orders by a few Japanese exporters was magnified by the extremely thin year-end market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It looks like there were still some exporters who must sell dollars," said Atsushi Hirano, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sales at \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Royal Bank of Scotland\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Later in the day, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will release its December \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  figure, which most Tokyo traders expect to be zero.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exporters also pushed the euro down against its Japanese counterpart. It was at Y100.32 at 0450 GMT, down from Y100.70 in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many Tokyo market participants said investors, especially in Europe, will try to push the euro below the psychologically important Y100.00 again. On Thursday, such an attempt was unsuccessful, with the unit rebounding after briefly touching Y100.05.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I'm sure the London guys will try the level again," said Hiroshi Maeba, a senior dealer at Nomura Securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the euro at Y100.00 would trigger for a large number of exotic option contracts, meaning flows from both buyers and sellers of these deals will intensify as the spot gets close to this point.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against the dollar, the euro was at $1.2942 from $1.2960. No major news or economic indicators are scheduled, so trading factors will likely be limited to share price movements, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the dollar fell to a record low against the Chinese yuan at CNY6.3070. Traders said the market reacted to Friday's central parity rate, which was CNY6.3009, the lowest rate on record.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The fixing surprised us, but most traders think it's politically motivated, partly as a friendly gesture to the U.S. for not labeling China a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator," said a Shanghai-based foreign bank trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said they expect the fixing to rebound next week, with the trading band likely be CNY6.3070 to CNY6.3130 for the time being.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 80.423 from 80.371.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par