\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: Japan Awaits New ECB  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Point Man With Optimism\b0\par\par\uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2011\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Japan hopeful that change at ECB may soften hard line against yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- Officials see potentially more sympathetic line from new chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Benoit Coeure\par \par \uc2 -- Analysts say diverse nature of ECB constituents makes any major change unlikely\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Stung by recent high-profile criticism from Washington, the Japanese government is hoping that a planned reshuffle of Europe's key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official next year could bring a more sympathetic ear to Japan's actions to weaken the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has stood as a major obstacle to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since the country resumed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in September 2010 to fight sharp yen rises that are doing damage to its export-dependent manufacturers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ECB joined a concerted step by the Group of Seven countries on March 18 to counter a jump in the yen, but it has been critical of other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  undertaken unilaterally by Tokyo. The bank appears to worry that such actions could encourage other nations--particularly China--to try to weaken their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ECB criticism was joined this week by opposition to Japan's moves by the U.S. Treasury, which said that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were not warranted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some Japanese government officials say the view from Europe may change once French Treasury official Benoit Coeure replaces Lorenzo Bini Smaghi as the top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy to the ECB president, a reshuffle due to take place on Jan. 1.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think Mr. Coeure will be less inflexible than Mr. Smaghi" on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy issues, a Japanese government official familiar with international finance issues told \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2  recently.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has traditionally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mainly in the dollar-yen market, but its success depends, in part at least, on European officials. If overseas officials are openly critical of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , this can serve as a signal to traders that the yen will likely resume its rise. This has become even more urgent after the negative comments from Washington.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coeure will become the counterpart of U.S. Treasury Undersecretary for International Affairs Lael Brainard and Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Takehiko Nakao.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I've never felt uncomfortable" with Coeure's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy views, a different Japanese government official said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fairly rare for a European policymaker, Coeure has a bachelor's degree in Japanese and speaks the language. He also was the head of France's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy unit in 2000, when Japan helped underpin a then-sinking euro through joint G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a jointly authored paper in 1999, "The Case Against Benign Neglect of Exchange Rate Stability," Coeure suggests that freely floating exchange rates can be imperfect.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But analysts say the collective decision-making style of the 17-nation \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could make it hard for Coeure to make any dramatic changes in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Makoto Utsumi, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs in 1989-1991, told Dow Jones that it is "probably difficult for any individual--even the bank's president--to give the ECB a whole new face."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since 2010, Japan has sold more than Y16 trillion in the market, mostly through solo actions. Stopping the yen from rising has become an important goal for the government as it tries to fight deflation and deal with the aftermath of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some Japanese government officials contend Bini Smaghi has refused to budge from an ideological opposition to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's solo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which they see as particularly galling in the view that Europe's debt crisis as a major reason for the yen's rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But an ECB spokesman, while offering no direct comment on Bini Smaghi's views, stressed that "the bank's policy is set by its decision-making bodies," not by any individual.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He added that the ECB's official stance toward Japan's solo steps remains what was stated by former President Jean-Claude Trichet on Aug. 4: "We consider that such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have to be made on the basis of a multilateral consensus and a multilateral decision ... To my knowledge what has been done is not part of a multilateral decision."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese and European divide underscores the difficulty of forming international consensus on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially at a time when many nations are seeking to boost exports. Weakening the yen could benefit Japan's exporters, but hurt their rivals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 29-12-11 0702GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4258 5095   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111229e7ct00086\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
