\par\par \b \uc2 DJ US Treasury Says Didn't Support Recent  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Currency Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tom Barkley   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2011\par 04:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--The U.S. Treasury said Tuesday it didn't support recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting Tokyo will continue to face international resistance to its efforts to cap the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 While U.S. officials had previously reacted coolly to bouts of unilateral yen-selling in August and October, the latest statement represents the strongest rebuke yet from the Obama administration of Japan's heavy-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. The comments come at a time when the U.S. is seeking to pressure China and other emerging Asian economies to shift to more market-driven exchange rates, an effort that has been complicated by Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Rather than reacting to domestic 'strong yen' concerns by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to influence the exchange rate, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should take fundamental and thoroughgoing steps to increase the dynamism of the domestic economy, increase the competitiveness of Japanese firms--including those in utilities and services--and raise potential growth," Treasury said in its semiannual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report to Congress.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, most of the report focused on China. While Treasury once again opted not to accuse Beijing of manipulating its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it called the pace of yuan appreciation "insufficient."\par \par \uc2 The strong language could cause Japan to hesitate to return to the market, said a senior dealer at a major bank in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "I won't say it will become impossible, but it may take them more time to get the green-light from the U.S. before staging another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the size of any campaigns ahead likely much smaller," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. and other Group of Seven nations joined \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the March 11 earthquake. But the U.S. and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  withheld support from Tokyo's more recent moves.\par \par \uc2 "In contrast to the G-7 joint post-earthquake \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, the United States did not support these \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Treasury said in Tuesday's report.\par \par \uc2 Disputing Japanese official views that the moves were aimed at damping speculation and calming disorderly markets, the report said markets appeared to be "orderly" and reacting to events beyond Japan. The dollar was trading with less volatility against the yen than it was against the euro at the time, it said.\par \par \uc2 That stance is also a shift from a Treasury report earlier in the year, which only noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September 2010.\par \par \uc2 -By Tom Barkley , \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 202-862-9275, tom.barkley@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Sudeep Reddy and Ian Talley in Washington, and Takashi Mochizuki in Tokyo, contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020111228e7cs001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
