\par\par \b \uc2 INDIAN MORNING BRIEFING: US Data Supports Asian Shares; Energy Stocks Mixed Despite Oil's Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 983 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2011\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL MARKETS \par DJIA          12291.35 -2.65   -0.02% \par Nasdaq        2625.20  +6.56   +0.25% \par S&P 500       1265.43  +0.10   +0.01% \par FTSE 100      5512.70  +55.73  +1.02% \par Nikkei Stock  8440.52  -0.04    0.00% \par Hang Seng     18518.13 -111.04 -0.60% \par Kospi         1824.35  -17.67  -0.96% \par  \par USD/JPY    77.84-86   -0.15% \par Range      78.02-77.80 \par EUR/USD    1.3066-68  +0.05% \par Range      1.3083-1.3044 \par  \par CBOT Wheat March  $6.446     a bushel \par Comex Gold        $1,595.50   -$10.50 \par Comex Gold Range  $1,591.10-$1,609.20 \par Nymex Crude (NY)  $101.34      +$1.66 \par  \par  \par US STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. blue-chip stocks' year-end rally ran out of steam Tuesday, slipping slightly to snap a four-session string of gains as investors weighed a better-than-expected reading on consumer confidence against crude oil's rise back above $100 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Crude-oil futures for February delivery shot up 1.7% to finish at $101.34 a barrel, a six-week high.\par \par \uc2 In a sign of continuing investor cautiousness, conservative utilities and telecommunications stocks led the day's gains. The utilities sector has been the best performer in the S&P 500 this year, gaining 15%.\par \par \uc2 Technology stocks were also strong. Intel and Cisco Systems led the gainers among Dow components, up 0.7% and 0.6% respectively.\par \par \uc2 Financial stocks pulling market indexes downward. \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  fell 2.1% and \uc2 J.P. Morgan Chase\uc2  dropped 1.6% to lead the Dow's decliners.\par \par \uc2 The moves in the holiday-shortened week came after a week in which the Dow gained 3.6%, including a 124-point rally Friday that sent the blue-chip index to a five-month high. The S&P 500 also moved back into positive territory for the year, and is up 0.6% with just three full sessions remaining in 2011.\par \par \uc2 "It was a real rollercoaster ride, but all things considered, it wasn't that bad a year for stocks--it could've been a lot worse given all the uncertainty and political headwinds," said Brian Gendreau, market strategist with Cetera Financial Group.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were down Wednesday as investors weighed U.S. economic data indicating improved consumer confidence against ongoing concerns over the debt crisis in Europe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro stayed rangebound ahead of a key Italian bond auction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is traditionally a good time of the year for equities, but we have EUR20 billion of Italian government debt being auctioned in the next two days, so there is some event risk which will probably cap any gains," said IG Markets institutional dealer Chris Weston.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data Tuesday showed U.S. consumer confidence hit an eight-month high in December.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Industrial Average futures were down 3 points in screen trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Energy-related plays in the region traded mixed despite oil futures Tuesday settling above the key $100 a barrel level for the first time in two weeks during U.S. trading, as Iran threatened to close the Strait of Hormuz--a vital crude-shipping route--if Western nations passed sanctions against its oil exports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inpex fell 0.3% in Tokyo, \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Innovation\f28 \uc2 \f2  was flat in Seoul, \f28 \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Oil & Gas\f28 \uc2 \f2  added 0.7% in Wellington and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woodside Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 0.8% in Sydney.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mining companies weighed the Australian market on a recent weakness in gold and spot iron-ore prices. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 1.2% while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Newcrest Mining\f28 \uc2 \f2  dropped 2.5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 14.2% on comments by Japanese Trade and Industry Minister Yukio Edano late Tuesday that the utility needs to fundamentally rebuild its finances, and that it should consider all options, including temporary state control.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro continued to trade in tight ranges against the U.S. dollar and the Japanese yen amid holiday-thinned volumes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors were also cautiously eyeing an Italian bond auction later in the day as a gauge of whether distressed government bonds will be purchased by European banks after the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's cash infusion last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at $1.3071 against the greenback from $1.3068 late Tuesday in New York and at Y101.66 versus the yen from Y101.77. The dollar was at Y77.79 from Y77.89.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold was at $1,587.70 a troy ounce, down $4.60 from its previous settlement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February Nymex crude oil futures were recently down 12 cents at $101.22 a barrel on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES \par US Consumer Confidence Jumps In December \par Obama To Name Two To Fill Fed Vacancies \par US Home Prices Decline In October \par Greece To Hold Elections At End Of April -Finance Minister \par Sears To Close Stores As Woes Continue \par Japan, China Leaders Focus On North Korea \par NYSE, Deutsche Boerse Extend Deal Deadline \par US Midwest Manufacturing Output Slips \par US Treasury Declines Once Again To Tag China As \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Manipulator \par ING Scraps Plan For Sale Of Belgian Insurance Unit \par GE To Buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Metlife Bank\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par Huawei CEO Divulges Leadership Structure \par China GPS System Begins Service \par S Korea Manufacturers' Outlook Index Falls To 29-Month Low \par Samsung, Sharp In LCD Price-Fixing Settlement \par US Criticizes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 Kobe Steel\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Partner With India's SAIL, Eyeing Plant Deal -Nikkei \par OSE, TSE To Give Merger Details By Summer, OSE President Says -Nikkei \par Mitsui To Invest In Major US Smart-Grid Project -Nikkei \par Canon Restarts Thai Inkjet Printer Plant -Nikkei \par Aeon, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Seven & I\f28 \uc2 \f2  Seen Reporting Record Pretax Profits -Nikkei \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Furukawa Electric\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Tap Local Partners In Chinese Cable Fray -Nikkei \par Japan's Electronic Parts Shipments Down 7% In October -Nikkei \par Takefuji's Sponsor Selection Back To Drawing Board -Nikkei \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 28-12-11 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62500   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020111228e7cs00002\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
