\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Update\b0\par\par\uc2 1,410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2011\par 01:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 US Dollar\par \par \uc2 U.S. Markets closed for holiday.\par \par \uc2 Euro\par \par \uc2 EUR/USD - to consolidate in higher range. Supported by positive risk sentiment. But EUR/USD topside limited by worries over euro-zone financial crisis; expectations that ratings firms will downgrade European sovereign debt; fear of euro-zone recession. EUR/USD daily chart positive-biased as stochastics bullish at oversold; MACD staged bullish crossover against its exponential moving average; though inside-day-range pattern completed yesterday. Resistance at 1.3082 (yesterday's high), then at 1.3095 (Friday's high) and 1.3120 (Thursday's high); breach would expose upside to 1.3199 (Wednesday's high), then 1.3212 (previous base set Nov. 25), 1.3237 (Dec. 13 high), 1.3388 (Dec. 12 high) and 1.3434 (Dec. 9 high). Support at 1.3039 (yesterday's low), then at 1.3026-1.3016 band (Friday's low-Thursday's low), 1.2993-1.2983 band (Dec. 20 low-Dec. 19 low), 1.2957 (Dec. 15 low) and 1.2945 (Dec. 14 11-month low); breach would expose downside to 1.2860 (Jan. 10 reaction low), then 1.2642 (Sept. 10, 2010 low), 1.2625 (Aug. 31, 2010 low) and 1.2588 (Aug. 24, 2010 swing low).\par \par \uc2 Japanese Yen\par \par \uc2 USD/JPY - to range-trade. Liquidity thin in Asia as markets in HK, Australia and NZ closed today for holiday. USD/JPY buoyed by yen-funded carry trades amid positive risk sentiment (Japan's Nikkei ended up 1% at 8,479.34 yesterday following Friday's strong finish on Wall Street) as recent U.S. economic data point to economic recovery and Congress approved tax-cut extension. USD/JPY also supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  importer demand, expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But USD/JPY topside limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  exporter sales. Data focus: 2350 GMT Japan December provisional trade statistics for 1st 10 days, November monetary policy meeting minutes, November corporate service price index, November import & export statistics, 0500 GMT Japan November construction orders & housing starts, 1330 GMT U.S. November Chicago Fed Midwest manufacturing index, 1400 GMT U.S. October S&P/Case-Shiller home price index, 1500 GMT December Richmond Fed business activity survey, U.S. December consumer confidence index, 1530 GMT U.S. December Texas manufacturing outlook survey. USD/JPY daily chart mixed as stochastics bearish at overbought, but MACD flat. Support at 77.87 (yesterday's low), then at 77.68-77.61 band (Wednesday's low-Dec. 16 low); breach would target 77.49 (Dec. 9 low, near 55-day moving average), then 77.13 (Dec. 8 low, matching 100-day moving average), 77.00-76.92 band (Nov. 24 low-Nov. 23 low) and 76.83-76.73 band (Nov. 22 low-Nov. 21 low). Resistance at 78.10 (yesterday's high), then at 78.23-78.29 band (Friday's high-Nov. 29 high); breach would target 78.41 (Nov. 2 high), then 78.98 (200-day moving average) and 79.55 (Oct. 31 high).\par \par \uc2 Sterling\par \par \uc2 GBP/USD - to consolidate in higher range. Supported by positive risk sentiment. But GBP/USD topside limited by GBP sales on buoyant EUR/GBP cross; worries over euro-zone debt crisis. Daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics in bearish mode. Resistance at 1.5645 (yesterday's high), then at 1.5707 (Friday's high) and 1.5727 (Thursday's high); breach would expose upside to 1.5773-1.5779 band (Wednesday's high-Nov. 30 high), then 1.5841 (100-day moving average), 1.5888 (Nov. 18 high) and 1.6052 (200-day moving average). Support at 1.5582 (Friday's low), then at 1.5545 (hourly chart); breach would expose downside to 1.5493 (Dec. 20 low), then 1.5463 (Dec. 19 low), 1.5432 (Dec. 15 low) and 1.5407 (Dec. 14 10-week low).\par \par \uc2 Swiss Franc\par \par \uc2 USD/CHF - to be range-bound. Undermined by broadly weaker demand for USD amid improved risk sentiment. But USD/CHF downside limited by expectations of \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's CHF-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Daily chart mixed as MACD & stochastics in bearish mod, but 5-day moving average flat. Support at 0.9337-0.9331 band (yesterday's low-Friday's low), then at 0.9305 (Thursday's low); breach would expose downside to 0.9240 (Wednesday's low), then 0.9174 (Dec. 8 low), 0.9161 (Dec. 5 low) and 0.9108 (Dec. 2 low, matching 55-day moving average). Resistance at 0.9388 (Friday's high), then at 0.9400 (Thursday's high) and 0.9414 (Dec. 16 high); breach would expose upside to 0.9548 (Dec. 15 high), then 0.9775-0.9785 band (Feb. 11 high-Jan. 11 high), 0.9915 (Dec. 8, 2010 high) and psychological 1.0000 level.\par \par \uc2 Canadian Dollar\par \par \uc2 USD/CAD - to consolidate in lower range. Undermined by positive risk sentiment; but downside limited by worries over euro-zone financial crisis. USD/CAD daily chart negative-biased as MACD & stochastics in bearish mode; 5-day moving average below 15-day MA and falling. Support at 1.0178 (yesterday's low, matching Friday's low); breach would expose downside to 1.0122 (100-day moving average), then 1.0049 (Dec. 8 low) and 0.9888 (Oct. 27 reaction low). Resistance at 1.0234 (yesterday's high), then at 1.0280 (Thursday's high) and 1.0308 (Wednesday's high); breach would expose upside to 1.0387 (Dec. 20 high), then 1.0414-1.0423 band (Dec. 19 high-Dec. 14 high), 1.0468 (Nov. 28 high), 1.0523 (Nov. 25 reaction high) and 1.0571 (Oct. 5 high).\par \par \uc2 Australian Dollar\par \par \uc2 AUD/USD to consolidate in higher range. Supported by positive risk sentiment, AUD-USD interest-rate differential, sovereign demand for Aussie. But AUD/USD gains tempered by worries over e