331. \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  fixed the dollar/yuan central parity rate at 6.3167, down from Friday's 6.3209. Offshore, the yuan rose against the dollar in the nondeliverable forwards market. One-year dollar-yuan nondeliverable forwards rose to 6.3790/6.3840 from 6.3755/6.3805 late Friday, and implying a 0.9% fall by the yuan against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the next year. The offshore yuan market in Hong Kong was closed for the Christmas holiday.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020111227e7cr00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
