\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro creeps lower on Europe funding fears\b0\par\par\uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2011\par 05:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Euro support holding above 11-mth nadir\par \par \uc2 * Euro could rise on short-covering\par \par \uc2 * Aussie hits session high on RBA minutes\par \par \uc2 By Lisa Twaronite\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 20 (Reuters) - The euro on Tuesday crept closer to an 11-month low hit last week, after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Mario Draghi quashed hopes for more aggressive bond purchases that have helped control European yields.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.3003, above an 11-month low of $1.2944 hit last week and a Monday session trough of $1.2983, but well off Monday's high of $1.3044.\par \par \uc2 Resistance lies at $1.3090, which would be a 50 percent retracement of its recent move to $1.2944 from $1.3236.\par \par \uc2 Draghi told the European Parliament on Monday that the ECB's purchases of peripheral debt were temporary and "not infinite", disappointing investors who were hoping for further bond buying that would keep yields stable. He also said 2012 will be a difficult year for the euro zone's banks, and recovery in economic activity in the region is likely to be slow.\par \par \uc2 Following a three-hour conference call, European Union finance ministers said they agreed on Monday to boost IMF resources by 150 billion euros ($195 billion) to ward off the debt crisis and won support for more money from EU allies.\par \par \uc2 But the EU said those lenders must first win parliamentary approval and Britain made it clear it would not participate, raising doubts about whether the group will be able to reach its 200 billion euro target.\par \par \uc2 "Concerns about the European situation will keep the euro under pressure even if it manages short-term rises," said Sumino Kamei, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 Some investors believe the euro could receive a brief lift on short-covering in thin conditions ahead of the year-end. IMM data released on Friday showed net short positions in the euro against the dollar totalled 116,457 as of Dec. 13.\par \par \uc2 The ECB's first three-year loan tender on Wednesday will also be closely watched and is expected to receive heavy bids. This could ease some fears about a dollar crunch for euro zone banks.\par \par \uc2 Euro zone banks are expected to buy some 250 billion euros, according to a Reuters poll, with forecasts widely ranging from 50 billion euros to 450 billion euros.\par \par \uc2 But with European leaders still trying to come up with measures to contain the region's debt crisis, any rise the euro has managed in recent weeks has been met with selling, and investors remain wary of further sovereign downgrades.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cut its debt rating for Belgium by two notches to Aa3 from Aa1, and Fitch warned it could may downgrade France and six other euro zone countries as it believes a comprehensive solution to the region's debt crisis is "technically and politically beyond reach".\par \par \uc2 COUNTERING WORRIES\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar stood at $0.9933, down from a session high of $0.9941 hit after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  (RBA) presented a balanced outlook in its policy meeting minutes, countering worries of some traders who were expecting a more dovish view.\par \par \uc2 The RBA chose to cut interest rates earlier this month because it felt the downside risks from Europe has increased, and it warned of slower global growth next year.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie stalled right ahead of moderate resistance at the bottom of the Ichimoku cloud on its hourly charts at $0.9945.\par \par \uc2 The dollar continued to receive safe-haven support after the death of North Korean leader Kim Jong-il raised questions about the leadership of the nuclear renegade state, though investors were seen unlikely to build new positions.\par \par \uc2 "Unless there is something new about the North Korean situation, Kim's death has already been factored in," Kamei said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index was down slightly at 80.326.\par \par \uc2 The greenback was steady against the yen at around 77.99 yen , but some strategists said thin conditions at the end of the year could nudge the pair out of its recent complacency.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar/yen tends to trade in a volatile way during the last three business days of the year, based on trading patterns in recent years," said Tohru Sasaki, head of Japan rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at JPMorgan Chase Bank in Tokyo.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  war chest to 195 trillion yen ($2.50 trillion), the government decided on Tuesday. The increase will be made in a fourth extra budget for the fiscal year to next March.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already spent roughly 128 trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so the increase would effectively mean it has some 67 trillion yen to spend, to stifle whatever it deemed to be excessive yen strength. ($1 = 0.7682 euros)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Antoni Slodkowski in Tokyo and Cecile Lefort in Sydney)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111220e7ck0005b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
