\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2011\par 08:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO BOOST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WAR CHEST BY Y30 TRILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government said Tuesday it will bolster its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war chest by Y30 trillion--the second biggest increase on record--a fresh sign of determination to prevent sharp yen rises from undermining the nation's fragile economic recovery. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA: TO ACTIVELY PARTICIPATE IN G-20 TALKS ON EXPANDING IMF RESOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government on Tuesday said it will actively participate in Group of 20 talks on expanding the International Monetary Fund's resources to deal with the euro-zone debt crisis. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA MARKETS RECOVER FROM N KOREA SHOCK; AUTHORITIES READY TO ACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's financial markets were staging a modest recovery Tuesday, retracing some of Monday's steep losses as investors digested the implications of North Korean dictator Kim Jong Il's death and the ensuing transfer of power. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECON MIN FURUKAWA: TO WORK WITH BOJ TO SAFEGUARD ECON, MARKETS AFTER KIM'S DEATH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Tuesday that the government and the Bank of Japan will work together to ensure the country's economy and financial markets are not damaged by any instability after the death of North Korean leader Kim Jong Il. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPE CRISIS WILL SET AGENDA FOR RBA RATES IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further cuts in Australian interest rates in 2012 look set to be decided mostly by the crisis in Europe, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or RBA, saying Tuesday the relative health of the local economy argued against cutting rates at its policy meeting on Dec. 6. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: GERMAN NOV PPI +0.1% ON MONTH; +5.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German factory prices edged up slightly in November but were in line with analysts' expectations, data from Germany's federal statistics office Destatis showed Tuesday. (published 2332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRENCH BUDGET MIN: HAS NO DOUBT BRITAIN WILL CONTRIBUTE TO IMF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French budget minister Valerie Pecresse said Tuesday she had no doubt Britain will end up joining a collective European Union effort to boost the International Monetary Fund Resources. (published 2335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S REMAINS NEGATIVE ON FINNISH BANKING SYSTEM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service said Tuesday its outlook for Finland's banking system remains negative as weak economic growth is likely to continue amid tough competition and vulnerable asset concentration. (published 2344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN JAN GFK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE KEEPS ROBUST ON LABOR MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German market research group GfK's forward-looking consumer confidence index is set to remain robust in January as labor market prospects in Germany continue to be strong, Reuters news agency said Tuesday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: SWISS NOVEMBER EXPORTS RISE 3.8% ON YEAR IN REAL TERMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swiss export growth slowed in November as the strength of the Swiss franc offset continued robust demand from Asia for the country's luxury goods and watches. (published 2300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S&P SEES ASIA-PACIFIC CREDIT OUTLOOK MODERATING IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia-Pacific economies and banks will be tested by a slowing global economy and a potential worsening of Europe's fiscal crisis, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report Tuesday. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO HAVE 103 ITEMS ON IMPORT TARIFF-CUT LIST IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance on Tuesday said it will have 103 items on its import tariff-cut list next year to stabilize price pressures and ease the financial burden on domestic industries. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PROPERTY TAX TO RAISE FUNDS, STABILIZE MARKET LONG TERM - RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although questions have been raised about the effectiveness of China's pilot property tax program, a government researcher said Tuesday the tax will eventually reduce market volatility and produce revenue for the state. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC PROFESSOR: CHINA MUST CONTINUE EXCHANGE RATE MECHANISM REFORMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recent fluctuations in yuan trading that caused the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to repeatedly fall by its daily limit against the U.S. dollar mainly reflect robust domestic demand for dollars and don't suggest that China should alter its course on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform, an academic with China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wrote in a commentary in the Shanghai Securities Journal Tuesday. (published 0159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA STARTS REGIONAL TRADING OF YUAN AGAINST THAI BAHT - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese authorities have started to allow regional trading of the yuan against the Thai Baht, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK GOVERNMENT, UNIONS MAKE PROGRESS IN PENSION TALKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. government and the country's largest trade union group said they had made progress in talks on reforming public sector pensions Monday, although unions stressed no agreements had been reached and there would be more discussion in the new year. (published 2308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE REBOUNDS SLIGHTLY IN NOV -NATIONWIDE SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer confidence in the U.K. recovered slightly in November, despite continued pessimism about the outlook for the economy and the jobs market. (published 0001 GMT) [ 20-12-11 0756GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111220e7ck000d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
