\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For December 20\b0\par\par\uc2 1,549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2011\par 08:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO BOOST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WAR CHEST BY Y30 TRILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government said Tuesday it will bolster its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war chest by Y30 trillion--the second biggest increase on record--a fresh sign of determination to prevent sharp yen rises from undermining the nation's fragile economic recovery. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA: TO ACTIVELY PARTICIPATE IN G-20 TALKS ON EXPANDING IMF RESOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government on Tuesday said it will actively participate in Group of 20 talks on expanding the International Monetary Fund's resources to deal with the euro-zone debt crisis. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA MARKETS RECOVER FROM N KOREA SHOCK; AUTHORITIES READY TO ACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's financial markets were staging a modest recovery Tuesday, retracing some of Monday's steep losses as investors digested the implications of North Korean dictator Kim Jong Il's death and the ensuing transfer of power. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ECON MIN FURUKAWA: TO WORK WITH BOJ TO SAFEGUARD ECON, MARKETS AFTER KIM'S DEATH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Tuesday that the government and the Bank of Japan will work together to ensure the country's economy and financial markets are not damaged by any instability after the death of North Korean leader Kim Jong Il. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS EUROPE BEHIND RATE CUT, BUT ECONOMY SOLID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The comments follow the release of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy-meeting minutes from Dec. 6 earlier today, in which it said Europe's debt crisis had fueled two interest rate cuts since November. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: EUROPE CRISIS WILL SET AGENDA FOR RBA RATES IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further cuts in Australian interest rates in 2012 look set to be decided mostly by the crisis in Europe, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or RBA, saying Tuesday the relative health of the local economy argued against cutting rates at its policy meeting on Dec. 6. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S&P SEES ASIA-PACIFIC CREDIT OUTLOOK MODERATING IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia-Pacific economies and banks will be tested by a slowing global economy and a potential worsening of Europe's fiscal crisis, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report Tuesday. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA TO HAVE 103 ITEMS ON IMPORT TARIFF-CUT LIST IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance on Tuesday said it will have 103 items on its import tariff-cut list next year to stabilize price pressures and ease the financial burden on domestic industries. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PROPERTY TAX TO RAISE FUNDS, STABILIZE MARKET LONG TERM - RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although questions have been raised about the effectiveness of China's pilot property tax program, a government researcher said Tuesday the tax will eventually reduce market volatility and produce revenue for the state. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC PROFESSOR: CHINA MUST CONTINUE EXCHANGE RATE MECHANISM REFORMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recent fluctuations in yuan trading that caused the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to repeatedly fall by its daily limit against the U.S. dollar mainly reflect robust domestic demand for dollars and don't suggest that China should alter its course on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform, an academic with China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wrote in a commentary in the Shanghai Securities Journal Tuesday. (published 0159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: CHINA MAY EASE MONETARY POLICY STANCE 2012 - RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may ease its "prudent" monetary policy stance to "neutral" or "moderately loose" in the coming year to prevent any sharp decline in the world's No. 2 economy, a researcher with a state-owned bank said. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STARTS REGIONAL TRADING OF YUAN AGAINST THAI BAHT - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese authorities have started to allow regional trading of the yuan against the Thai Baht, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: THAI NOV CUSTOMS-BASIS TRADE DEFICIT $1.37 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's trade deficit widened in November to $1.37 billion from $1.01 billion a month earlier, due mainly to reduced exports of manufactured goods after the country's worst flood in decades disrupted production, the Ministry of Commerce said Tuesday. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: YANZHOU, GLOUCESTER IN TALKS TO CREATE A$8B COAL MINER-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yanzhou Coal Mining Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is in initial talks with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gloucester Coal Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to merge their Australian coal assets and create a miner worth up to 8 billion Australian dollars, three people familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LI & FUNG\f28 \uc2 \f2  CONTROLLING FAMILY OFFERS TO BUY HANG TEN FOR US$340.7 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A company owned by the Fung family, which controls blue chip trading firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li & Fung Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., is offering to buy apparel firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Ten Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for US$340.7 million. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: APPLE WINS ROUND AGAINST HTC, ANDROID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . was handed a legal victory that is bad news for rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., as a U.S. trade agency ruled that some \f28 \uc2 \f2 HTC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . smartphones that use the Internet company's Android software infringe an Apple patent. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: HITACHI PRESIDENT "CONCERNED" ABOUT DELAYS IN SALE OF HARD DISK DRIVE OPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The president of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hitachi Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday he is "very concerned" about possible further delays in the planned sale of its hard disk drive business to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Western Digital Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . beyond March, as the U.S. company has yet to gain approval from various international regulators. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MACMAHON HOLDINGS\f28 \uc2 \f2  UPGRADES FY12 EARNINGS GUIDANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macmahon Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it expects full year net profit for the 2012 financial year to be more than 55 million Australian dollars . (published 2147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GUODIAN TECHNOLOGY: REDUCED HK IPO TO US$303 MLN FROM UP TO US$646 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Guodian Technology & Environment Group Corp. said Tuesday it reduced the size of its Hong Kong initial public offering to US$303 million from its previous plan to raise up to US$646 million. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KT CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2 : FORMS CONSORTIUM WITH 13 MOBILE OPERATORS FOR ASIA SUBMARINE CABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KT Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's largest fixed-line operator and second-largest mobile carrier by revenue after \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Telecom Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Tuesday that it has formed a consortium with 13 global mobile operators, including Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 NTT Communications Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., to develop an Asian submarine cable. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA ASSET PICKS BARCLAYS, SAMSUNG SECURITIES TO ADVISE ON KYOBO LIFE STAKE SALE - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run bad-debt bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Asset Management Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has selected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Securities Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to advise on the planned sale of a stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kyobo Life Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., in a deal valued around KRW400 billion, a person with direct knowledge of the matter said Tuesday. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WESTPAC FACES CLASS ACTION OVER FEES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Westpac Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Tuesday said it has received a legal claim alleging that some of the fees it charged customers prior to October 2009 were unlawful. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: GROWTHPOINT TO BUY PROPERTY FOR A$289.5 MLN; PLANS RIGHTS OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growthpoint Properties Australia Ltd. said Tuesday it has bought three office properties in Brisbane and an office development site in Sydney for 289.5 million Australian dollars to be part funded by an underwritten A$166.4 million rights issue at A$1.90 a share. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: DELL: TO SELL SMARTPHONE WITH BAIDU SOFTWARE PLATFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dell Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it would start selling a smartphone in China using a software platform developed by Chinese search-engine operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Baidu Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: COCHLEAR IDENTIFIES CAUSE OF IMPLANT FAILURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cochlear Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday hearing implant failures that led to the voluntary recall of its unimplanted Nucleus CI500 series were caused by microcracks in a joint that let water into the device. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; SEOUL REBOUNDS, BUT REGIONAL MOOD CAUTIOUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian stock markets were modestly higher Tuesday, amid scattered deal-making and receding worries the death of North Korean leader Kim Jong Il might spur instability on the Korean Peninsula, but Europe's continuing debt crisis tempered gains. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA CABINET PROPOSES LIFTING VAT ON VEGETABLE DISTRIBUTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China proposes to lift a value-added tax on the distribution of vegetables as part of a larger plan to contain inflation by improving the network of agricultural product distribution, the executive office of the country's cabinet said in a statement Tuesday. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA GOVERNMENT: FOOD PRICES ROSE LAST WEEK, LED BY VEGETABLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's food prices rose in the week to Sunday, with vegetable prices up 7.9% during the sixth consecutive week of increases, the Ministry of Commerce said in a statement Tuesday. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA GOVERNMENT: NEW SOUTH WALES WHEAT CROP DAMAGED BY RAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rainfall has damaged some winter crops including wheat and delayed the end of a relatively large annual harvest in New South Wales state, the Department of Agriculture reported Tuesday in an occasional Grains Report. (published 0018 GMT) [ 20-12-11 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111220e7ck000am\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
