\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2011\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO BOOST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WAR CHEST BY Y30 TRILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government said Tuesday it will bolster its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war chest by Y30 trillion--the second biggest increase on record--a fresh sign of determination to prevent sharp yen rises from undermining the nation's fragile economic recovery. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA: TO ACTIVELY PARTICIPATE IN G-20 TALKS ON EXPANDING IMF RESOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government on Tuesday said it will actively participate in Group of 20 talks on expanding the International Monetary Fund's resources to deal with the euro-zone debt crisis. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA MARKETS RECOVER FROM N KOREA SHOCK; AUTHORITIES READY TO ACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's financial markets were staging a modest recovery Tuesday, retracing some of Monday's steep losses as investors digested the implications of North Korean dictator Kim Jong Il's death and the ensuing transfer of power. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECON MIN FURUKAWA: TO WORK WITH BOJ TO SAFEGUARD ECON, MARKETS AFTER KIM'S DEATH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Tuesday that the government and the Bank of Japan will work together to ensure the country's economy and financial markets are not damaged by any instability after the death of North Korean leader Kim Jong Il. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS EUROPE BEHIND RATE CUT, BUT ECONOMY SOLID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The comments follow the release of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy-meeting minutes from Dec. 6 earlier today, in which it said Europe's debt crisis had fueled two interest rate cuts since November. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: EUROPE CRISIS WILL SET AGENDA FOR RBA RATES IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further cuts in Australian interest rates in 2012 look set to be decided mostly by the crisis in Europe, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or RBA, saying Tuesday the relative health of the local economy argued against cutting rates at its policy meeting on Dec. 6. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S&P SEES ASIA-PACIFIC CREDIT OUTLOOK MODERATING IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia-Pacific economies and banks will be tested by a slowing global economy and a potential worsening of Europe's fiscal crisis, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report Tuesday. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO HAVE 103 ITEMS ON IMPORT TARIFF-CUT LIST IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance on Tuesday said it will have 103 items on its import tariff-cut list next year to stabilize price pressures and ease the financial burden on domestic industries. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PROPERTY TAX TO RAISE FUNDS, STABILIZE MARKET LONG TERM - RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although questions have been raised about the effectiveness of China's pilot property tax program, a government researcher said Tuesday the tax will eventually reduce market volatility and produce revenue for the state. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC PROFESSOR: CHINA MUST CONTINUE EXCHANGE RATE MECHANISM REFORMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recent fluctuations in yuan trading that caused the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to repeatedly fall by its daily limit against the U.S. dollar mainly reflect robust domestic demand for dollars and don't suggest that China should alter its course on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform, an academic with China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wrote in a commentary in the Shanghai Securities Journal Tuesday. (published 0159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: CHINA MAY EASE MONETARY POLICY STANCE 2012 - RESEARCHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may ease its "prudent" monetary policy stance to "neutral" or "moderately loose" in the coming year to prevent any sharp decline in the world's No. 2 economy, a researcher with a state-owned bank said. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA STARTS REGIONAL TRADING OF YUAN AGAINST THAI BAHT - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese authorities have started to allow regional trading of the yuan against the Thai Baht, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: THAI NOV CUSTOMS-BASIS TRADE DEFICIT $1.37 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's trade deficit widened in November to $1.37 billion from $1.01 billion a month earlier, due mainly to reduced exports of manufactured goods after the country's worst flood in decades disrupted production, the Ministry of Commerce said Tuesday. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: UK GOVERNMENT, UNIONS MAKE PROGRESS IN PENSION TALKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. government and the country's largest trade union group said they had made progress in talks on reforming public sector pensions Monday, although unions stressed no agreements had been reached and there would be more discussion in the new year. (published 2308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE REBOUNDS SLIGHTLY IN NOV -NATIONWIDE SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer confidence in the U.K. recovered slightly in November, despite continued pessimism about the outlook for the economy and the jobs market. (published 0001 GMT) [ 20-12-11 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111220e7ck000a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
