\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 4-BOJ tankan shows Japan business mood worsening\b0\par\par\uc2 805 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2011\par 01:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 15 (Reuters) - Japanese business sentiment worsened in the three months to December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tankan survey showed, as a stubbornly strong yen, Europe's debt crisis and slowing global growth clouded the country's recovery prospects.  *************************************************************\par \par \uc2  KEY POINTS:\par \par \uc2  -- The headline index for big manufacturers' sentiment worsened to minus 4 in December from plus 2 in September. The median estimate was for a reading of minus 2. \par \par \uc2  -- Big non-manufacturers' sentiment improved to plus 4 from plus 1 in September, against a median market forecast for a reading of plus 1.\par \par \uc2  -- The index for March next year was seen at minus 5 for big manufacturers and 0 for big non-manufacturers.\par \par \uc2  -- Big firms cut their capital expenditure plans for the year to next March to a 1.4 percent increase from a 3.0 percent gain projected in the previous survey in September, against a median forecast for a 2.5 percent increase.\par \par \uc2  -- Big manufacturers expect the dollar to average 79.02 yen\par \par \uc2 in the fiscal year to March 2012, the strongest yen level expected since comparable data became available in 1996.\par \par \uc2  -- Sentiment at large automankers improved for the second straight quarter.\par \par \uc2  COMMENTARY:\par \par \uc2  YOSHIKIYO SHIMAMINE, EXECUTIVE CHIEF ECONOMIST, DAI-ICHI LIFE RESEARCH INSTITUTE, TOKYO\par \par \uc2  "Companies are taking more cautious views of the economy due to the one-two punch of the slowdown in overseas economies and the firmer yen.\par \par \uc2  "Given the likelihood that overseas economies including those of emerging nations will slow further, we should be aware of the risk of big manufacturers' sentiment towards the business outlook worsening more . \par \par \uc2  "Since what Japan can do to support the economy is limited in terms of fiscal policies, the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  should seek more drastic easing steps."\par \par \uc2  GEORGE WORTHINGTON, IFR MARKETS CHIEF ECONOMIST, SYDNEY\par \par \uc2  "The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's quarterly Tankan survey showed manufacturers becoming pessimistic thanks to the worsening global outlook, even as non-manufacturers, more dependent on the domestic market, became marginally more optimistic.\par \par \uc2  "The survey is not bad enough to spur the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  into taking more active measures to support the economy, but points to another sub-par year for the domestic economy."\par \par \uc2  HIROKAI MUTO, SENIOR ECONOMIST, SUMITOMO MITSUI ASSET MANAGEMENT CO, TOKYO\par \par \uc2  "Sentiment at electronics makers is weak as they are adjusting inventories. Automaker sentiment is likely to weaken from here on due to the strong yen and as the boost from the recovery in supply chains wanes.\par \par \uc2  "This tankan report also shows signs of weak overseas demand.\par \par \uc2  "I thought capital expenditure was holding up, but now we can see that this is weakening too.\par \par \uc2  "I think the BOJ will be slightly shocked by this tankan. I think the BOJ will continue to increase asset purchases, but it's more a matter of timing. If the dollar broke toward 76 yen, then the BOJ might buy more assets to coordinate with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2  TATSUSHI SHIKANO, SENIOR ECONOMIST, MITSUBISHI UFJ MORGAN STANLEY SECURITIES\par \par \uc2  "Europe's debt crisis, the yen's rise and the Thai floods dealt a blow to manufacturing sentiment. Companies are cautious about risks from Europe's problems and a strong yen in the coming months, and these factors are weighing on their capital spending.\par \par \uc2  "That said, I expect the world economy to resume picking up next year once Europe's sovereign debt crisis subsides. The Bank of Japan must be very cautious about its outlook but it is likely to stand pat on monetary policy for the time being unless a sudden spike in the yen triggers a plunge in share prices."\par \par \uc2  MARKET REACTION:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -- For yen updates click, for prices click \tab \par  -- For JGB updates click, for prices click \tab \par  -- For stocks click, for the Nikkei click \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  LINKS:\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  For a full table of the survey, click:\tab \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boj.or.jp/en/statistics/tk/gaiyo/2011/tka1112.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boj.or.jp/en/statistics/tk/gaiyo/2011/tka1112.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2  BACKGROUND:\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  -- Japan's economy rebounded from a recession triggered by\par the March earthquake and tsunami, but is expected to slow\par sharply this quarter as the initial spurt driven by companies\par restoring supply chains and production facilities tails off.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  -- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and eased\par monetary policy in October to reduce the pain from sharp yen\par rises and slowing overseas growth. The BOJ kept monetary\par settings unchanged last month but has signalled its readiness to\par ease again if the economy's recovery comes under threat. It\par holds its next policy meeting on Dec. 20-21.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  -- The tankan indexes are derived by subtracting the\par percentage of respondents who say conditions are poor from those\par who say they are good. A negative reading in the diffusion index\par indicates pessimists outnumbered optimists.\tab \par \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara, Rie Ishiguro, Kaori Kaneko,\par Tetsushi Kajimoto, Stanley White, Tomasz Janowski, Kiyoshi\par Takenaka; Editing by Joseph Radford)\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/TANKAN (INSTANT VIEW 4)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111215e7cf0000q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
