\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  FOCUS: And Then There Was One...\b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2011\par 12:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's resolute defense of euro/franc floor has effectively closed off one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven\par \par \uc2 -- Bank of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  action has been bit less dramatic\par \par \uc2 -- Investors say BoJ could step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By David Cottle\par \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--It used to be so simple.\par \par \uc2 When \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors felt panicky, they headed to, or back to, old faithfuls: the Swiss franc, the U.S. dollar and the Japanese yen. This was at the expense of riskier units--yes, euro, we can see you--and those judged too exposed to global growth, such as the Australian or Canadian dollars.\par \par \uc2 However, in September this trade proved too worrisome at least for Zurich. Swiss business was getting very uncomfortable with the strength of the franc, so the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the forthright step of pledging to defend a floor of CHF1.20 against the euro, with 'unlimited' selling of its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This effectively shooed the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets' refugees out of their Swiss haven.\par \par \uc2 So, one old faithful down. Two left.\par \par \uc2 Now Japan has been at least as worried about the strength of the yen but, as their worries center on its exchange rate with the dollar, and Washington is extremely twitchy about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation, especially when other people do it, Tokyo has been a bit less forthright in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions.\par \par \uc2 It has, however, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets, selling a considerable size of yen in an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the end of October. This has been estimated to have been of the order of a gargantuan $120 billions' worth.\par \par \uc2 Now, analysts at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  say, investors are becoming more certain that they'll see more such action, and that the yen's haven status will increasingly come under question.\par \par \uc2 "Several signals indicate that market participants are becoming less convinced that the yen can maintain this status, on fears of extended Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb further yen strength," the bank wrote.\par \par \uc2 The bank says there are signs in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  option market, as well as in its own sentiment indicators, that investors no longer expect yen gains if, for example, the euro crisis worsens.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Lloyds Corporate Markets in London struck a similar note Friday, noting the yen's rise against the dollar with other 'risk on' assets in the wake of comments from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the list of haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2012 will be a short one indeed: the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg TNI FRX POV\par \par \uc2 Reuters USD/DJ\par \par \uc2 Thomson P/1066 or P/1074\par \par \uc2 (David Cottle is a Special Writer for Dow Jones Newswires, contributing to the Wall Street Journal. He has reported on corporate credit, the U.K. economy and the sovereign debt markets for Dow Jones Newswires. He has also edited, and written for, the company's Market Talk product in London and Singapore. He can be reached at +44 20 7842 9436 or david.cottle@dowjones.com) [ 09-12-11 1157GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1066   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111209e7c9000qj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
