\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 1-OECD calls for 'aggressive' ECB action on debt crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2011\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * ECB bond-buying in crisis is not moral hazard - OECD's Tamaki\par \par \uc2  * EU leaders must show unity towards fiscal integration\par \par \uc2  * Germany must overcome public sentiment to revolve crisis\par \par \uc2  * G7 not objecting to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background, details)\par \par \uc2  By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to take aggressive action and the European Union must aim for fiscal solidarity to resolve the region's debt crisis, a senior official at the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development said on Friday.\par \par \uc2  Rintaro Tamaki, a deputy secretary-general of the OECD, made the remarks a day after ECB President Mario Draghi signalled it stood ready to act more aggressively to fight Europe's debt crisis if political leaders agree next week on much tighter budget controls in the 17-nation euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Two years into Europe's debt crisis, investors are fleeing the euro zone bond market, European banks are dumping government debt, south European banks are bleeding deposits and a recession looms, fuelling doubts about the survival of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  To resolve the debt crisis, Tamaki, who served as Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official for two years until August, urged Germany to overcome domestic opposition to EU fiscal solidarity and aggressive action by the ECB.\par \par \uc2  "It is obvious that neither aggressive ECB action nor each European country's institutional enhancement towards fiscal integration can be achieved without Germany changing its stance," Tamaki told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2  "Germany must make the proper judgment and demonstrate clear leadership by overcoming public sentiment to break through the current situation."\par \par \uc2  The ECB's bond buying is justifiable at a time of crisis, he added.\par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan is buying yen-denominated bonds and the Fed is buying dollar-denominated bonds as a monetary adjustment tool under normal conditions," he said.\par \par \uc2  "I don't think you call it a 'moral hazard' when a crisis hits and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rescues its own country's bond market from the brink of collapse."\par \par \uc2  The euro zone's debt crisis has become the biggest threat to the global economy and a break-up of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bloc can no longer be ruled out, the OECD said on Monday, slashing its forecasts and urging the ECB to play a bigger role in defusing the crisis.  \par \par \uc2  The crisis has led to the yen's strengthening driven by safe-haven fund flows, jeopardising Japan's recovery from the March earthquake.\par \par \uc2  In Tamaki's tenure as vice finance minister for international affairs, he oversaw Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice -- once on its own September last year and once jointly with G7 countries following the March earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least twice solo since then.\par \par \uc2  Tamaki said it would be a waste of time to argue whether Japan's action has gained understanding from other countries.\par \par \uc2  "The G7 has not objected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... There is no such argument as 'never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' or 'it's okay to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  all the time'," Tamaki said.\par \par \uc2  "What we have agreed is that excess volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is negative for the economy."\par \par \uc2  Tamaki currently oversees programmes covering financial affairs, taxes, environment, development and green growth, at the OECD, a Paris-based think-tank. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-OECD/TAMAKI (INTERVIEW, UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111205e7c2000ga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
