\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: Swiss KOF Drop Signals Sharp Slowdown -\uc2 UniCredit\b0\par\par\uc2 1,623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 11:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1054 GMT [Dow Jones] The slide in Swizterland's November KOF leading indicator is further evidence of a sharp slowdown in the economy, though it should steer clear of a recession, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Given the strong franc and weaker European demand, then the decline is understandable," according to economist Alexander Koch. "We expect a mild contraction in 1Q Swiss GDP, but no full-blown recession, although the risks lie to the downside," he notes. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1051 GMT [Dow Jones] Turkey's trade deficit kept widening in October as the slowdown in imports remained limited, says Ekspres Invest. The trade deficit came in at US$8.0B in October, in line with the consensus yet visibly above Ekspres' $6.5B call, says an analyst. "We prefer to remain cautious given the fact that the small size drops in the current account deficit are not enough to bring around a major change in the risk perception about Turkey's external gap," adds the analyst. Even if the economy slows next year, any narrowing in the current account deficit may be limited in the lack of structural reforms, given the fact that imports will be moderating from a very high base and that export performance is to remain sluggish amidst the turbulence in Europe, the analyst says. (yeliz.candemir@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1051 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds are higher, as bullish cut-offs in a T-bill auction provide further fuel for the rally sparked by the RBI's bond buyback announcement late Tuesday and muted 2Q GDP growth data. The benchmark 8.79% 2021 bond is at 100.37, the intraday high, from 99.76 at Tuesday's close. But a dealer with a privately-run bank says most of the positives have been priced in and the benchmark yield is unlikely to fall below 8.70% in the short-term. Traders will also be watching out for the cut-offs in the RBI's bond buyback Thursday, with some expecting the RBI to buy fewer bonds than in a buyback last week, he says. He tips the 8.79% 2021 bond in a 8.70%-8.80% band this week; the yield is at 8.73%.(sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1046 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish GDP growth forecast uncertainty very high says BPH as the scale of the economy slowdown in Poland "will be predominantly shaped by the situation in the euro area," says Adam Antoniak, Senior Economist at \uc2 Bank BPH\uc2  in Warsaw. BPH's baseline scenario assumes "the worst-case scenario for the euro area is averted". In that scenario, the bank forecasts Poland's economy will expand at a 3.2% rate in 2012. Still, "the scale of uncertainty is exceptionally high..." and the risk is Polish growth will undershoot rather than overshoot this projection. Poland's statistics office said Wednesday GDP rose 4.2% in 3Q vs 4.3% in 2Q. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1043 GMT [Dow Jones] Yuan deposits in Hong Kong dropped 0.6% in October, the first decline in two years, suggesting a stabilization of investor sentiment toward the offshore yuan, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says, adding the decline of yuan deposits is less than the bank expected. "Given the limited use for CNH offshore to-date, the primary demand to buy and hold CNH offshore comes from savers and investors. A sharp deterioration in sentiment and thus investor demand would lead to a sharp imbalance between supply and demand," the report says. "The lack of a bigger decline in October's deposit base suggests to us that the stabilization of CNH.... (is) due more to a stabilization of investor sentiment towards the offshore yuan, than to a rapid net uptake of cross-border channels to buy the cheaper offshore yuan to remit back onshore," the house says. "In sum, the fact that CNH deposits and trade settlement activity only declined modestly gives some comfort about the overall resilience of the offshore yuan system, as a vehicle for yuan internationalization," \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1040 GMT [Dow Jones] The amount of yen Japanese authorities sold to curb JPY strength was large, but justifiable given the campaign was conducted amid global market turmoil, says Daisuke Karakama, a market economist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2 . Japan MOF data showed the Japanese government sold Y9.092 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Oct. 28 to Nov. 28. The efforts to tame the JPY's strength are seen as effective as it helped lift the USD/JPY to around 78.00 from the record low of 75.31 marked Oct. 31, Karakama says. "Most everyone was saying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't be effective, but I insist that the fact that selling orders from Japanese exporters were cleared away because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had a significant meaning." The USD/JPY hasn't trended lower over the last few days even though it is the month-end, when the USD/JPY tends to decline due to selling from Japanese exporters. "The huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign was effective," he says. The USD/JPY is at 78.14. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1039 GMT [Dow Jones] Norway retail sales stronger than expected says SEB after data show seasonally adjusted retail sales, excluding motor vehicles, rose 0.8% in October from a month earlier. Much of the gains down to sales of household equipment like furniture and electrical appliances, SEB says. Looking ahead says the recent warm weather and the delay in winter conditions could be a negative for retail sales. It will "likely put a lid on sales of seasonal clothes and sporting goods in November and probably December," SEB says. (charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1030 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  expects the Spanish Treasury to be able to raise the minimum targeted amounts at its bond auction Thursday. "Support from domestic investors, Securities Markets Program purchases (ECB bond buy) and month-end index changes should enable the Treasury to raise the minimum amount on offer," it says. Spain plans to raise EUR2.75 billion to EUR3.75 billion in 2015, 2016 and 2017-dated bonds. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1019 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan's MOF might have secretly sold more than Y1 trillion between Nov. 1 and Nov. 4, judging from data just released showing Japan spent more than Y9 trillion between Oct. 28 and Nov. 28, says Izuru Kato, chief economist in Tokyo at the money-market brokerage Totan. "It's very likely that they have done it," he says, adding "I believe there were no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Nov. 7." \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Senior Vice Finance Minister Igarashi had no comment on whether the MOF conducted stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the questioned period. The pair is at 78.03. (takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1019 GMT [Dow Jones] The monetary-easing policies of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are no longer having a negative impact on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 . "In fact, we believe that the BRL is now attractive on a relative value basis, having underperformed over the past week," \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  says. Future rate cuts are already priced in and, if anything, the market is overpricing cuts over the next few months, which could support BRL, it adds. Later Wednesday, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cut the Selic rate 50bps to 11%. "The rationale behind the earlier cut remains relevant in our view, and there is no fundamental reason why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should alter its policy stance at this stage." USD/BRL trades at 1.8455.(clare.connaghan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1015 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end up 0.7% at 995.33 with buying in laggard PTT-group stocks propelling the market; trade is thin. Investors shrug off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 25bp rate cut to 3.25% as it was in line with the market expectations. "The Thai stock market is likely to move in a range amid an absence of fresh drivers. Profit-taking will emerge when the SET index nears the 1000 resistance, while buys on dip help limit downside," says \uc2 Thanachart Securities\uc2  Assistant Vice President Noppadol Piriyawut. Support is put at 980. Among the most active shares, \uc2 PTT Global Chemical\uc2  (PTTGC.TH) rises 2.3% to THB65.50, PTT (PTT.TH) gains 2.0% to THB306, True (TRUE.TH) is up 2.6% at THB3.18, \uc2 Thai Airways International\uc2  (THAI.TH) is down 1.0% at THB19 and Thai Oil (TOP.TH) is up 0.8% at THB61.25. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT [Dow Jones] India swaps are lower across the curve after the RBI announced another bond buyback late Tuesday, while a muted GDP reading for July-September strengthens the case for further monetary easing. The one-year OIS are at 8.06%/8.08% vs 8.09%/8.11% late Tuesday, while the five-year OIS are at 7.29%/7.32% vs 7.31%/7.33%. A dealer with a privately-run bank advises receiving across the curve, although traders will have to watch out for the negative carry between the one-year swap rate and the overnight rate. "The market is expecting more OMOs (open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) from the RBI, which should weigh on the front-end of the curve, and the subdued outlook on (India's) GDP growth is also likely to push the back-end lower," he adds, tipping one-year swaps in a 8.0%-8.12% range this week. (sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 30, 2011 05:54 ET (10:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111130e7bu0034t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
