\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  data points to 1 trln yen "stealth"  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in Nov\b0\par\par\uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold record Y9 trln in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in month to Nov 28\par \par \uc2  * Points to Y1 trln stealth selling in wake of huge Oct 31 move\par \par \uc2  * Fin Min Azumi declines to confirm covert selling\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has about 37 trln yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ammunition\par \par \uc2  * Full \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  details due in February \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background, comments)\par \par \uc2  By Hideyuki Sano\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably sold about 1 trillion yen in small-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the days after a massive bout of yen selling on Oct 31 to stem the yen's gains to a record high against the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry said it spent a record 9.09 trillion yen ($115 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the month to Nov 28, as it tried desperately to stem the yen's rise, which hurts export-dependent Japan. \par \par \uc2  As Japan is estimated to have spent nearly 8 trillion yen on Oct 31 alone, a daily record, the announcement suggests the ministry spent about 1 trillion yen in the days that followed in follow-up action probably intended to keep markets more on edge for fear of more big moves.\par \par \uc2  Sources have said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  stealthily in the week of Oct. 31-Nov. 4 in a move widely seen as an attempt to make sure the impact of the huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 31 did not fade.\par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities said on that day that they needed to act against speculative market moves, and Finance Minister Jun Azumi said authorities would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until they were satisfied.  \par \par \uc2  But officials have declined to comment on whether they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Oct. 31, and Azumi declined to comment after Wednesday's data on whether there had been any stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "While the data is not rock-solid proof they did stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , today's announcement is in line with what many market players have felt, that there was covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Since Oct. 31, the dollar has stayed above its record low of 75.31 yen hit just hours before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began. It traded at 78.02 yen on Wednesday, 3.6 percent above the record low.\par \par \uc2  That may count as a modest success for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given that after its previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Aug 4, when it spent what was then a record 4.5 trillion yen, the dollar gave up all of the gains in just three days.  \par \par \uc2  Japan also used another new tactic in the latest bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by keeping the dollar stuck at 79.20 yen for a few hours on Oct. 31, sparking some speculation the authorities may be thinking of introducing a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg like the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did in early September.\par \par \uc2  But few believe Japan will follow in the footsteps of the Swiss as that would run counter to Group of Seven (G7) efforts on China to let the yuan trading more flexible.\par \par \uc2  In fact, many market players think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was first and foremost aimed at giving Japanese exporters breathing space to sell the dollar at a better rate.\par \par \uc2  As many Japanese exporters struggle with a combination of a slowing global economy and a stronger yen, market players expect Japan to step into the market again should the dollar fall to around the 75 yen mark.\par \par \uc2  In theory, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has sizable ammunition for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The government won parliamentary approval this month to raise its borrowing limit for future yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 15 trillion yen, topping up its coffers to around 37 trillion yen.\par \par \uc2  Still, many market players do not think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a lasting impact on a market in which roughly $4 trillion changes hands every day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has fallen to current lows from 308 yen before the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1973, despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since then.      \par \par \uc2   Full details of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this quarter, including what \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it sold on each day, will be published in February. \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Sumio Ito; Editing by Joseph Radford and Hugh Lawson)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111203e7bu0009j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
