\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  May Have Conducted Stealth  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Data Suggest\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 11:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- MOF data suggest \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely conducted stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November\par \par \uc2 -- Announced Oct. 31 campaign likely largest-ever single day \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- Dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics could become more opaque\par \par \uc2 TOKYO -- The Japanese government may have secretly continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after its huge yen-selling campaign on Oct. 31, data released Wednesday suggest, in a sign that Tokyo may be changing its tactics against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \uc2 The data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  show the government spent Y9.092 trillion on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Oct. 28 and Nov. 28. That was far more than the roughly Y7.68 trillion--a single day record--that analysts estimate Tokyo sold in the market during its announced Oct. 31 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar fell to a fresh record low of Y75.31.\par \par \uc2 "It's likely Japan secretly sold more than Y1 trillion between Nov. 1 and Nov. 4," said Izuru Kato, chief economist in Tokyo at the money-market brokerage Totan.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's data only show the total monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figure, and so do not prove that the MOF secretly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets after Oct. 31. Investors must wait until the ministry releases a detailed report broken down by day and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair in February for confirmation.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, it would suggest a new tactic for trying to weaken the yen, mixing highly public forays into the market with stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave investors uncertain over what may come next, with the aim of making its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  more effective.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors say that the ministry was almost certainly active in the market after Oct. 31.\par \par \uc2 In early November, a major bank was "oddly and constantly" placing yen-selling orders a bit below Y78.00, indicating that the bank was acting as an agent of the BOJ, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. The BOJ conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  under instruction from the MOF.\par \par \uc2 "If we think about market demand at that time, the dollar should have easily fallen below Y77.50 if nothing abnormal was going on," the dealer said. Between Nov. 1 and Nov. 4, the greenback traded in a range between Y77.89 and Y79.10.\par \par \uc2 People familiar with the government's thinking hinted that such speculation is correct, saying Japanese authorities obtained a green-light for stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from their U.S. and European counterparts in return for buying European Financial Stability Facility bonds and joining talks on the Trans-Pacific Partnership.\par \par \uc2 As of 1000 GMT, the dollar was at Y78.04.\par \par \uc2 Traders think that the MOF hasn't conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last few weeks, but Finance Minister Jun Azumi has said recently that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if market moves become excessive.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ, meanwhile, has surveyed banks in Tokyo on how they might help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market during New York and London trading hours. Some consider this to be a form of "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " aimed at creating the impression that action may be imminent.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the authorities may step into the market if the dollar falls to a Y75-76 range, adding that Tokyo's tactics may become even more opaque--by picking banks outside of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  as agents for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for example, or by striking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options deals or adopting computer-based trading.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's data suggest the campaign on Oct. 31, which lasted until New York trading hours, was the largest-ever single-day \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The previous record was on Aug. 4, when the MOF sold Y4.513 trillion for dollars.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 11-30-11 0555ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111130e7bu0003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
