\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Nishimura: European Debt Crisis Biggest Risk For Japan Econ Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 03:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 KYOTO, Japan (Dow Jones)--Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Wednesday that the ongoing euro-zone debt crisis is the biggest risk factor for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's baseline scenario that the Japanese economy will eventually return to a sustainable growth path.\par \par \uc2 "Needless to say, the risk factor that should cause most concern is future developments in the sovereign debt problem in Europe and their effects on global financial markets and the global economy," Nishimura told business leaders in Kyoto, western Japan.\par \par \uc2 "The debt problem has largely affected the global economy already, but it could result in weaker growth, not only in the European economy but also in the global economy, particularly through its effects on global financial markets," he said.\par \par \uc2 Nishimura is scheduled to hold a press conference from 0440 GMT.\par \par \uc2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com [ 30-11-11 0221GMT ]\par \par \uc2 KYOTO, Japan (Dow Jones)--Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Wednesday that the government's latest yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effective and pledged to remain on guard against any further negative economic impact from the strong yen.\par \par \uc2 "Rather than the direct impact on exchange rates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  played a very important role in showing the authorities' stance of not tolerating excessive (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) moves," Nishimura said at a press conference after meeting business leaders in Kyoto, western \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tokyo conducted an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign on Oct. 31 after the dollar hit a fresh record low of Y75.31. As of 0522 GMT, the dollar was at Y77.89.\par \par \uc2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com [ 30-11-11 0523GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111130e7bu00046\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
