\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ BOJ Shirakawa: Japan Econ Expected To Face Difficult Situation For While, Particularly Exports\b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2011\par 03:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:36 EDT *DJ  BOJ Shirakawa: BOJ Will Continue To Implement Powerful Credit Easing To Ensure Sustainable Recovery\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:36 EDT *DJ  BOJ Shirakawa: Powerful Credit Easing Reflects Sense Of Crisis Vs Econ Dnside Risks\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:37 EDT *DJ  BOJ Shirakawa Reiterates European Soverign Debt Crisis Biggest Risk For Japan Econ\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:38 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Negative Feedback Loop Between Debt Situation, Fincl Sys, Real Econ In Europe Now In Place\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:38 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: BOJ Will Continue To Keep In Close Contact With Other Major Central Banks To Stabilize Mkt\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:39 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Japan Banks Not Facing Dollar-Funding Difficulties, But Global Shocks Could Have Impact\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:40 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Addressing European Sovereign Debt Problem Most Effective Way To Erase Yen's Rise\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:40 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Japan Econ Could Be Under Pressure From Negative Element For A While\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:40 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Need To Be Alert That Yen's Rise Could Pose Downside Risk By Damping Corp Pfts, Sentiment\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:41 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Risk That Continued Yen Strength May Accelerate Pace Of Firms Shifting Ops Overseas\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:41 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Japan Cos Have Failed To Boost Investment Despite Aggressive BOJ Credit Easing\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:42 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Mkt Properly, Steps Had Certain Impact\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:42 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Yen's Rise Has Both Merits And Demerits\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:44 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Raising So-Called Econ "Body Temperature" Could Be Answer To Overcome Deflation\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 21:44 EDT *DJ  BOJ Gov: Biggest Task For Japan Econ Is To Strengthen Growth Potential\par \par \uc2 27 Nov 2011 22:23 EDT DJ  BOJ Shirakawa: Japan Econ Expected To Face Difficult Situation For While\par \par \uc2 NAGOYA, Japan (Dow Jones)--Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Monday the Japanese economy could face a difficult situation for a while, as the European debt crisis, the yen's continued strength and the flooding in Thailand could take a toll on exports.\par \par \uc2 "The Japanese economy is expected to continue facing a severe situation for the time being, particularly with respect to exports," Shirakawa said at a meeting with business leaders in Nagoya, central Japan.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa reiterated that the biggest risk is the European sovereign debt crisis, as there is a negative feedback loop between the fiscal situation, the financial system, and the real economy.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ chief acknowledged the yen's rise could have an adverse impact on the export-oriented economy in the Nagoya area, the home of \uc2 Toyota Motor Corp\uc2 . (7203.TO) and its related companies. He said the strong yen could threaten the economy by slashing corporate profits and damping corporate sentiment, as well as accelerating the shift of manufacturing overseas.\par \par \uc2 "We are well aware that the yen's strength will have an adverse impact on companies and economy in that region," he said.\par \par \uc2 Aggressive credit easing that the BOJ has conducted reflects "a sense of crisis" about the economy, he said, pledging that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its easy policy to ensure the economy returns to a sustainable growth path.\par \par \uc2 Business executives at the meeting expressed concern about the yen's strength, which erodes their profits overseas when converted to yen, and threatens the competitiveness of their manufacturing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose as high as Y79.55 after large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities Oct. 31. But the euro-zone debt crisis has continued to put upward pressure on the yen, which is regarded as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 0310 GMT, the dollar was at Y77.63.\par \par \uc2 At its policy-setting meeting earlier this month, the BOJ decided to maintain the size of its asset buying program--regarded as the main tool for credit easing amid close-to-zero interest rates--at Y55 trillion. It boosted the fund by Y5 trillion in October.\par \par \uc2 -By Tatsuo Ito, Dow Jones Newswires; +813-6269-2780; tatsuo.ito@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 27, 2011 22:23 ET (03:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111128e7bs000pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
