\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2011\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF SPOKESPERSON: NO DISCUSSIONS WITH ITALY ON IMF FINANCING PROGRAM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund denied Monday that it is in talks with Italy to prepare a major bailout for the Group of Seven nation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD CUTS 2012 US GDP GROWTH FORECAST, SEES RECESSION IN EURO ZONE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The global economic outlook has deteriorated significantly, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said Monday, as it urged the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to act more decisively to prevent the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis from deepening further. (published 1000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD URGES BOLDNESS FROM ECB, GOVERNMENTS TO END CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should loosen monetary policy again and may need to devise more radical "non-standard" measures to save the euro-zone economy, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said in its Economic Outlook for 2012 published Monday. (published 1000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD PROJECTS US GDP TO GROW 2.0% IN 2012; 2.5% IN 2013 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The spending cuts and tax increases set to take place following the Congressional debt committee's failure and continued troubles in Europe could push the U.S. economy to the brink of recession, the Organisation for Economic Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Development said in its semi-annual economic outlook released Monday. (published 1000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD URGES BOE TO INCREASE QE AS UK ENTERS RECESSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England should increase its bond-buying stimulus program by GBP125 billion as the U.K. economy contracts in the first half of 2012, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said Monday. (published 1000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SNB'S HILDEBRAND: SWISS FRANC STILL "HIGHLY VALUED" - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss franc will be around for a long time and is still "highly valued," Swiss National Bank President Philipp Hildebrand says in an interview published Monday. (published 1138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: LAUNCH OF IMF NEW CREDIT LINE POSITIVE FOR STRESSED EURO-ZONE SOVEREIGNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund's launch of a new credit facility is positive for euro-zone sovereigns facing short-term funding problems, but can't alone solve the bloc's "escalating" crisis, Moody's Investors Service said Monday in its Weekly Credit Outlook report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: PROBABILITY OF MULTIPLE DEFAULTS BY EURO-ZONE COUNTRIES NO LONGER NEGLIGIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The probability of a series of defaults by euro-zone countries is no longer negligible, Moody's Investors Service warned Monday, noting that the longer the liquidity crisis continues, the more rapidly the risk of default would rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: INCREASING BANK RELIANCE ON ECB LIQUIDITY SUPPORT IS CREDIT NEGATIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone banks' growing reliance on financing from the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is credit negative and illustrates that the crisis is weakening the credit of financial institutions, Moody's Investors Service said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD: JAPAN ECONOMIC RECOVERY MODERATING DUE TO STRONG YEN, GLOBAL SLOWDOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economic growth, which had picked up due to public and private sector reconstruction spending following the March earthquake, is again falling back as the strong yen and weak global growth cut into exports, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said Monday. (published 1000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD: SEE ROOM FOR CHINA INTEREST-RATE CUTS BY MID 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in China is set to slow further, opening the door for interest-rate cuts by the middle of next year, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said Monday. (published 1000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU ALMUNIA: ECB IS INSTITUTION OF LAST RESORT DURING CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has to act as the institution of last resort to confront the euro zone's sovereign debt crisis, European Union Competition Commissioner Joaquin Almunia said Monday, in the latest sign of sustained pressure on the ECB to do more to help struggling economies like Spain and Italy. (published 1056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN, FRENCH, ITALIAN BANK CDS FALL BACK FROM RECORDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring the debt of core European financial companies against default fell Monday amid news that Italy will release a comprehensive fiscal bill Dec. 5 and hopes that Belgium is near agreeing a deal to form a new government. (published 1056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK NOV SALES VOLUME WEAKEST SINCE MARCH 2009 - CBI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales volume at U.K. retailers slumped to the lowest level since March 2009 in November, another sign that the U.K. economy is teetering on the brink of recession, a survey by the Confederation of British Industry showed Monday. (published 1102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: ECB: PRIVATE SECTOR LOAN GROWTH RISES IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--Euro-zone bank lending in October rose at a faster pace in annual terms than the previous month, data from the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Monday. The data suggest that, at least on a yearly comparison, banks are still willing to lend, despite fears of an economic slowdown from the intensifying debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALY BUSINESS CONFIDENCE INCHES UP IN NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROME (Dow Jones)--Italy's business confidence index unexpectedly rose in November, inching up on the back of hopes of improved prospects in the consumer-goods industry, national statistics institute Istat said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: INDIAN RESTRAINT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IS CREDIT POSITIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Indian government's restraint in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the rupee is credit positive, Moody's Investors Service said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SENIOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF OFFICIAL:NOT RULING OUT POSSIBILITY OF SOLO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 "There's no reason that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be regarded as a safe-haven," given its own fiscal problems and slow pace of growth, Takehiko Nakao, Vice Minister of Finance for international affairs, said at the Paris Europlace International Financial Forum held in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: SAXONY NOVEMBER CPI -0.1% M/M; +2.6% Y/Y \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--Consumer prices in the eastern German state of Saxony fell on the month in November, as price declines in leisure activities more than offset a slight increase in food prices, data from the state statistics office showed Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOV SAYS JAPAN ECONOMY FACING SEVERE PRESSURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Monday that the European debt crisis, along with the yen's continued rise, will likely put the Japanese economy in a severe situation, and he urged Europe to take bold actions to avoid a repetition of the 2008 global financial crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMANY WEIGHS IDEA OF CORE EURO-ZONE BONDS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany is weighing the idea of joining with five other core euro-zone member states to issue common bonds in order to stabilize their high credit rating, German daily Die Welt reported Monday, citing sources close to the negotiations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: CONCENTRATING MINDS IN BERLIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is nothing like fear to focus the mind. (published 1150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MONEY TALKS: TWO STEPS FORWARD, ONE STEP BACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another day another blunderbuss permanent solution to save the euro zone forever and to stave off panic. (published 1125 GMT) [ 28-11-11 1200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111128e7bs000rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
