\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2011\par 10:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF SPOKESPERSON: NO DISCUSSIONS WITH ITALY ON IMF FINANCING PROGRAM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund denied Monday that it is in talks with Italy to prepare a major bailout for the Group of Seven nation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S: LAUNCH OF IMF NEW CREDIT LINE POSITIVE FOR STRESSED EURO-ZONE SOVEREIGNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund's launch of a new credit facility is positive for euro-zone sovereigns facing short-term funding problems, but can't alone solve the bloc's "escalating" crisis, Moody's Investors Service said Monday in its Weekly Credit Outlook report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S: PROBABILITY OF MULTIPLE DEFAULTS BY EURO-ZONE COUNTRIES NO LONGER NEGLIGIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The probability of a series of defaults by euro-zone countries is no longer negligible, Moody's Investors Service warned Monday, noting that the longer the liquidity crisis continues, the more rapidly the risk of default would rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S: INCREASING BANK RELIANCE ON ECB LIQUIDITY SUPPORT IS CREDIT NEGATIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone banks' growing reliance on financing from the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is credit negative and illustrates that the crisis is weakening the credit of financial institutions, Moody's Investors Service said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: ECB: PRIVATE SECTOR LOAN GROWTH RISES IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--Euro-zone bank lending in October rose at a faster pace in annual terms than the previous month, data from the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Monday. The data suggest that, at least on a yearly comparison, banks are still willing to lend, despite fears of an economic slowdown from the intensifying debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY BUSINESS CONFIDENCE INCHES UP IN NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROME (Dow Jones)--Italy's business confidence index unexpectedly rose in November, inching up on the back of hopes of improved prospects in the consumer-goods industry, national statistics institute Istat said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S: INDIAN RESTRAINT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IS CREDIT POSITIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Indian government's restraint in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the rupee is credit positive, Moody's Investors Service said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SENIOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF OFFICIAL:NOT RULING OUT POSSIBILITY OF SOLO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 "There's no reason that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be regarded as a safe-haven," given its own fiscal problems and slow pace of growth, Takehiko Nakao, Vice Minister of Finance for international affairs, said at the Paris Europlace International Financial Forum held in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: SAXONY NOVEMBER CPI -0.1% M/M; +2.6% Y/Y \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--Consumer prices in the eastern German state of Saxony fell on the month in November, as price declines in leisure activities more than offset a slight increase in food prices, data from the state statistics office showed Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ GOV SAYS JAPAN ECONOMY FACING SEVERE PRESSURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Monday that the European debt crisis, along with the yen's continued rise, will likely put the Japanese economy in a severe situation, and he urged Europe to take bold actions to avoid a repetition of the 2008 global financial crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA GOVERNMENT: EXPECT INFLATION TO STABILIZE FROM 2H 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance Monday said it expects inflation to stabilize from the second half of 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA 3Q OVERSEAS INVESTMENTS DOWN 34.7% ON EURO-ZONE WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's third-quarter total overseas investments fell sharply from a year earlier, as companies cut spending amid heightened external uncertainties stemming from the euro-zone fiscal crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMANY WEIGHS IDEA OF CORE EURO-ZONE BONDS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany is weighing the idea of joining with five other core euro-zone member states to issue common bonds in order to stabilize their high credit rating, German daily Die Welt reported Monday, citing sources close to the negotiations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB NOYER BACKS EFSF LEVERAGE SCHEME FOR EURO MARKET LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Christian Noyer warned against central banks overstepping their primary mandate of maintaining mid-term price stability, with non-European central banks having gone on a public debt purchasing spree to provide liquidity to markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA VICE PREMIER: CHANCE OF LONG-TERM ECONOMIC WEAKNESS HAS RISEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chance of long-term global economic weakness has risen, Chinese Vice Premier Li Keqiang said in remarks published on a government website Monday, noting the spiralling European sovereign debt crisis, unstable international financial markets and slowing growth combined with price rises in some countries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA TO RELEASE MID-YR ECONOMIC, FISCAL OUTLOOK TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's government plans to release its 2011-12 Mid-Year Economic And Fiscal Outlook at 0000 GMT Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: THAI INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION INDEX -35.8% ON YEAR IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial production index plunged 35.8% in October compared with the same month a year earlier, as severe flooding hurt the country's manufacturing industry, the Ministry of Industry's Office of Industrial Economics said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 28-11-11 0957GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111128e7bs000mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
