\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 28\b0\par\par\uc2 1,538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2011\par 08:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SENIOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF OFFICIAL:NOT RULING OUT POSSIBILITY OF SOLO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 "There's no reason that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be regarded as a safe-haven," given its own fiscal problems and slow pace of growth, Takehiko Nakao, Vice Minister of Finance for international affairs, said at the Paris Europlace International Financial Forum held in Tokyo. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BOJ GOV SAYS JAPAN ECONOMY FACING SEVERE PRESSURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Monday that the European debt crisis, along with the yen's continued rise, will likely put the Japanese economy in a severe situation, and he urged Europe to take bold actions to avoid a repetition of the 2008 global financial crisis. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVERNMENT: EXPECT INFLATION TO STABILIZE FROM 2H 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance Monday said it expects inflation to stabilize from the second half of 2012. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA 3Q OVERSEAS INVESTMENTS DOWN 34.7% ON EURO-ZONE WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's third-quarter total overseas investments fell sharply from a year earlier, as companies cut spending amid heightened external uncertainties stemming from the euro-zone fiscal crisis. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA VICE PREMIER: CHANCE OF LONG-TERM ECONOMIC WEAKNESS HAS RISEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chance of long-term global economic weakness has risen, Chinese Vice Premier Li Keqiang said in remarks published on a government website Monday, noting the spiralling European sovereign debt crisis, unstable international financial markets and slowing growth combined with price rises in some countries. (published 0122 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA TO RELEASE MID-YR ECONOMIC, FISCAL OUTLOOK TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's government plans to release its 2011-12 Mid-Year Economic And Fiscal Outlook at 0000 GMT Tuesday. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: THAI INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION INDEX -35.8% ON YEAR IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial production index plunged 35.8% in October compared with the same month a year earlier, as severe flooding hurt the country's manufacturing industry, the Ministry of Industry's Office of Industrial Economics said Monday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI MOF: 2011 GDP GROWTH LIKELY IN 1.7%-2.0% RANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's economic growth this year will likely be in a range of 1.7%-2.0%, much lower than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's previous forecast of 3.8%-4.3% growth in late September, mainly because of adverse effects from the country's worst floods in decades, said Somchai Sujjapongse, head of the ministry's Fiscal Policy Office. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE GDP RISES 3.2% ON YEAR, SLOWER THAN MARKET'S 4.6% ESTIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine economy expanded 3.2% year-on-year in the third quarter, slower than expected due to bad weather, the higher cost of fuel, weak exports and a sluggish construction sector, raising the possibility that the country's gross domestic product will miss the government's full-year target of 4.5%-5.5% despite recent stimulus spending. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: KOREA NOVEMBER EXPORTS LIKELY REBOUNDED; CPI LIKELY ABOVE BOK TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's exports growth likely rebounded in November but inflation for the month likely exceeded the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target of 2% to 4% for the year, presenting difficult policy choices for Seoul as it faces heightened external uncertainties. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW CHINA LIFE SECURES FOUR INVESTORS AS CORNERSTONE INVESTORS TO BUY IN US$780 MLN IN DUAL LISTING - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New China Life Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has secured cornerstone investors to buy in a combined US$780 million worth of shares for its Hong Kong tranche of its around US$3 billion Hong Kong and Shanghai initial public offering, people familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GREAT EASTERN HOLDINGS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO INVEST US$380M IN NEW CHINA LIFE HK OFFERING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-listed insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Great Eastern Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it will invest US$380 million in the cornerstone tranche of Beijing-headquartered New China Life Insurance Co.'s Hong Kong share offering. (published 2337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PCCW HKT TRUST'S IPO RETAIL TRANCHE UNDERSUBSCRIBED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The initial public offering of \f28 \uc2 \f2 HKT Trust & HKT Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the telecommunications trust spun off from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PCCW Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., drew a lukewarm response from retail investors, who subscribed to just over a tenth of the shares on offer in the deal's retail portion, according to allotment results released Monday. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: STRIKES, FLEET GROUNDING TO HIT QANTAS PROFIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday forecast a steep decline in first half profit, largely driven by costly industrial action and the controversial grounding of its entire fleet to force a resolution with trade unions. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RIO RAMPS UP IRON ORE OUTPUT, WARNS CUSTOMERS CAUTIOUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has lifted its target for iron ore production out of Australia's remote Pilbara region despite Monday cautioning its customers are becoming increasingly cautious in the face of global economic uncertainty. (published 2245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO EXPECTS ALUMINUM UNIT TO BREAK EVEN IN SECOND HALF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that it expects underlying earnings at its aluminum division to hit break-even for the second half of the year, a sharp decline from the first six months due in part to higher raw material costs. (published 0020 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BHP BILLITON TAPS KERR TO SUCCEED VANSELOW AS CFO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday announced the surprise departure of Chief Financial Officer Alex Vanselow after more than five years in the role and said he would be succeeded in the new year by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Graham Kerr\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of its diamonds division. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA POLYMETALLIC MINING TO RAISE UP TO US$163 MLN IN HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Polymetallic Mining Ltd. plans to raise up to US$163 million in an initial public offering ahead of a Dec. 14 listing on the Hong Kong stock exchange, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 0225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA LIFESTYLE FOOD TO RAISE US$96 MLN IN HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Lifestyle Food & Beverages Group Ltd. plans to raise US$96 million in an initial public offering ahead of a listing on the Hong Kong stock exchange on Dec. 9, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SONY EXEC: WILL KEEP IMAGE SENSOR CORE MANUFACTURING TECHNOLOGY AT JAPAN PLANTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s components and professional devices division said Monday it will keep its core manufacturing technology for image sensors in Japan, despite the yen's persistent strength. (published 0405 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2 : AUSTRALIA UNIT GOT OK FROM COAL & ALLIED SHAREHOLDERS FOR PURCHASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese trading house \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its Sydney-based unit, along with and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , received approval from the shareholders of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coal & Allied Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to go ahead with the joint purchase of shares they don't currently own in the Australian coal producer. (published 0423 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHARTER GROUP POSTPONES UP-TO-US$350 MLN HK IPO ROADSHOW - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Charter Group Holdings Ltd. has postponed its roadshow for a Hong Kong initial public offering which could raise US$300 million-US$350 million due to market volatility, people familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ICBC RAISES STAKE IN ASSET MANAGEMENT JV UNIT TO 80% FROM 55% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial & Commercial Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ltd. has increased its holdings in its joint venture asset-management unit with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  to 80% from 55%, the unit said Saturday. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES, EURO RISE ON SOME EUROPE RELIEF; MARKETS STILL WARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets rallied and the euro rose on Monday, as investors cheered a surge in U.S. retail spending and weekend reports the International Monetary Fund could lend Italy a financial helping hand. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP BILLITON SEES CHINA STEEL OUTPUT HOLDING BELOW HISTORICAL HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Steel production in China is expected to continue at levels below historical highs for some time, which is being reflected in the lower price for iron ore, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marius Kloppers\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S BREAD BASKET FACES WATER SQUEEZE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A scheme to save water in Australia's key food producing region is pitching farmers against environmentalists and threatening to endanger the long-term future of the country's bread basket. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO: SHIFT TO SHORTER TERM IRON ORE PRICING CONTINUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The push to increasingly shorter term prices by buyers of iron ore continues, and the trend is unlikely to reverse, the head of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's iron ore division said Monday. (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA PLANS TO ALLOW STATE-RUN TRADING FIRMS TO EXPORT WHEAT, RICE - OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is planning to allow state-run trading companies to export wheat and common-grade rice from the local market to boost their earnings by tapping the global market, two food ministry officials said Monday. (published 0552 GMT) [ 28-11-11 0714GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111128e7bs000c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\p