\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 964 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2011\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SENIOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF OFFICIAL:NOT RULING OUT POSSIBILITY OF SOLO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 "There's no reason that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be regarded as a safe-haven," given its own fiscal problems and slow pace of growth, Takehiko Nakao, Vice Minister of Finance for international affairs, said at the Paris Europlace International Financial Forum held in Tokyo. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: EUROPE LEADERS ARE NEGOTIATING NEW FISCAL TIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's leaders are negotiating a ground-breaking fiscal pact aimed at preventing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc from fracturing by tethering its members even closer together. (published 0041 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: MONTI TO PROPOSE NEW ITALIAN AUSTERITY MEASURES - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian Prime Minister Mario Monti will propose billions of euros in new austerity measures next week--according to a person familiar with the matter--to reinforce Italy's pledge to balance its budget by 2013, a key part of its efforts to restore investor confidence in the country. (published 2159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW RULES FOR EFSF READIED FOR EURO-ZONE MEETING TUESDAY -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New rules for the European Financial Stability Facility would allow for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the primary and secondary bond markets and would see the fund offering partial protection to investors, Reuters reports on its website Sunday. (published 2041 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB NOYER: EFSF INCREASE UNREALISTIC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council member Christian Noyer said Monday that an increase in the European Financial Stability Fund would be unrealistic, but he's open to any scheme that would allow existing commitment to be leveraged to provide greater \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capacity. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MORGAN STANLEY SAYS US DOLLAR, YEN TO STRENGTHEN IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar and Japanese yen will gain steadily against all crosses in the coming year as global deleveraging continues, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a research report Monday. (published 2242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: US JOB MARKET LOOKING MORE LIKE EUROPE'S \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the U.S. tries to dodge the fallout from Europe's debt crisis, some economists are reaching a troubling conclusion: The American labor market is looking more European than ever. (published 0111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA VICE PREMIER: CHANCE OF LONG-TERM ECONOMIC WEAKNESS HAS RISEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chance of long-term global economic weakness has risen, Chinese Vice Premier Li Keqiang said in remarks published on a government website Monday, noting the spiralling European sovereign debt crisis, unstable international financial markets and slowing growth combined with price rises in some countries. (published 0122 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINESE RESEARCHER: CHINA'S GROWTH SLOWDOWN WILL BE MILD -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic-growth slowdown will be mild as investments are unlikely fall sharply in the near term and consumption will expand steadily, the official People's Daily reported Monday, citing a senior Chinese researcher. (published 2346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA ECONOMIST: SEE CPI RISE AROUND 4% IN 2012 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer price index growth is likely to be around 5.5% in 2011 but will likely fall to around 4% in 2012, the Financial News reported Monday, citing Fan Jianping, an economist at the National Development and Reform Commission's state information center. (published 0057 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: \f28 \uc2 \f2 DEUTSCHE BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTS DIM SUM BOND GROWTH TO SLOW 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in the market for offshore yuan-denominated bonds is likely to slow next year, as investors dial down their expectations about how much further the yuan will appreciate, a top banker from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. (published 0102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: GROWTH SLOWING IN SECOND HALF OF YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Monday once again warned of slowing economic momentum in the second half of the year on heightened external uncertainties, noting slowing exports and deteriorating domestic sentiment. (published 2313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA DECEMBER MANUFACTURERS' OUTLOOK INDEX 83 VS 82 NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean manufacturers' business outlook improved slightly in December, but remained weak due to the uncertain global economic outlook, a survey by the Bank of Korea showed Monday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINES 3Q GDP +3.2% ON YEAR; MARKET EXPECTED +4.6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine economy expanded 3.2% in the third quarter from a year earlier, with unfavorable weather conditions, higher fuel prices and sluggish construction slowing domestic growth, the National Statistical Coordination Board said Monday. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND NBNZ NOVEMBER BUSINESS CONFIDENCE +18.3%; OCT +13.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand business confidence improved slightly in November, a leading survey showed Monday. (published 0004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA XLX FERTILISER TO SELL ABOUT CNY324 MLN YUAN CONVERTIBLE BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China XLX Fertiliser Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it plans to sell around CNY324 million worth of yuan-denominated convertible bonds to a China-based private investment firm. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par WSJ(11/28) HEARD ON THE STREET: OVERHEARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If you hold a chart of the South African rand's 2010 performance versus the dollar against the same for the year to date in 2011, you get a picture of a global investment community that has swung sharply from risk appetite to risk aversion. (published 0225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: PROWLING BOND VIGILANTES SHOULD STRESS OUT BIG US BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banks are notoriously complex. But in one respect, they are pretty simple; like other companies, banks depend on access to a raw material to build products and need to purchase it at a price that allows them to generate a profit. (published 2101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FOCUS: UK GOVT SEEKS BOOST FOR GROWTH IN CREDIT EASING PACKAGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. government Tuesday will set out a range of schemes designed to revive growth in an already weak economy that now faces a number of headwinds from the euro zone, including the prospect of falling demand for its exports and reduced access to affordable funding for its banks. (published 1708 GMT) [ 28-11-11 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111128e7bs0004c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shp