\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2011\par 03:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: CAREFULLY MONITORING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Friday he has been carefully watching movements in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets since the ministry \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month, and reiterated that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will again take steps if there are speculative movements. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN OCT CORE CPI -0.1% ON YEAR; MKT EXPECTED -0.1% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's core consumer price index fell in October for the first time since June, according to government data released Friday, as last year's hikes in tobacco tax and nonlife insurance premiums tapered off. (published 2335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN CABINET OFFICE: GOVT TO WORK CLOSELY WITH BOJ TO DEAL WITH DOWNSIDE RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Cabinet Office on Friday said the government would work closely with the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in dealing with potential downside risks to the economy in the wake of the ongoing sovereign debt crisis in Europe. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SEES NOVEMBER CPI IN 4.5%-5.4% RANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday higher electricity rates and increases in food prices because of recent typhoons will likely keep the inflation rate elevated in November but that shouldn't affect monetary policy. (published 2302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: ECB'S PARAMO: GOVTS CAN'T EXPECT ECB TO FINANCE DEFICITS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cannot be a lender of last resort to governments -- and calls for it serve in that role are motivated by self-interest, ECB board member Jose Manuel Gonzalez Paramo said Thursday. (published 2300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA'S CIC MAY GIVE EUROPE 'INDIRECT' SUPPORT - BLOOMBERG NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the country's sovereign wealth fund, said it may help Europe tackle its debt crisis through "indirect" means, Bloomberg News reported Friday, citing Jesse Wang, the fund's executive vice president. (published 0052 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par XINHUA: EURO-ZONE BONDS MIGHT HELP SOLVE DEBT CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European countries issuing joint "euro-zone bonds" could help solve the region's sovereign debt crisis by lowering financing costs for heavily indebted countries like Greece, China's state-run Xinhua news agency said in a commentary late Thursday. (published 0058 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: EUROPE MUST FOLLOW THROUGH ON CRISIS MEASURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan Friday urged euro-zone countries to follow through on their plans to bring the sovereign debt crisis under control, voicing concerns about the current crisis developing into a full-fledged global crisis. (published 0045 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA GOVERNMENT, BOK: GROWTH IN HOUSEHOLD DEBT CONTINUES TO SLOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government and Bank of Korea on Friday said growth in household debt continues to slow, indicating that the government's efforts to manage debt levels are showing results. (published 0032 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: MOODY'S DOWNGRADES HUNGARY BONDS TO BA1 WITH NEGATIVE OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday downgraded Hungary's government bonds by a notch to Ba1 with a negative outlook, the ratings firm said. (published 0007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINES SEPTEMBER IMPORTS $5.13 BLN, +12% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The value of Philippine imports rose 12% year-on-year in September to $5.13 billion despite a continuing decline in the shipments of electronic products, the National Statistics Office said Friday. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BAOSTEEL SELLS CNY3.6 BLN DIM SUM BONDS THURSDAY - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Baosteel Group Corp. on Thursday sold CNY3.6 billion of offshore yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Friday, marking Beijing's latest effort to boost the nascent offshore yuan bond market as China moves to internationalize its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0026 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par WSJ: YEN MAY STILL BE TOO STRONG FOR BOJ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is three weeks since the Bank of Japan's blockbuster bout of yen-selling forced the dollar from the all-time lows it was then hitting against the rampant Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 1855 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: INSURERS PILE ON SOVEREIGN DEBT GLOOM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The law of unintended consequences continues to wreak havoc in the euro zone. Caught in the middle of a desperate banking sector deposit war, Europe's insurers are pulling back from savings markets in Italy, France and Spain. That in turn reduces their demand for sovereign bonds, adding to concerns over government funding - which increases pressure on the banks. (published 1833 GMT) [ 25-11-11 0201GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111125e7bp00031\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
