\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  FOCUS: The Return Of The Terminator\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2011\par 12:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Deflation, downgrade threats will have little impact\par \par \uc2 --Yen still seen as safe haven as global economy slows\par \par \uc2 --Investment flows still very much driver of yen\par \par \uc2 By Nicholas Hastings\par \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The yen is back.\par \par \uc2 Massive deficits haven't hurt. A shrinking trade surplus, no problem. Years of ZIRP just bounced off. Billions of quantitative easing made no difference. And now, the return of deflation. That won't matter either.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably bounce back even stronger than before.\par \par \uc2 This Terminator of the financial markets just doesn't operate like other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there is little sign that that will change.\par \par \uc2 At the moment, the yen is suffering from a bit of a weak spot as European banks liquidate their holdings in the Japanese government bond market as well as Japanese equities to cover their losses at home.\par \par \uc2 A warning from Standard & Poors Corp. about another downgrade because of the rise in Japanese bond yields hasn't helped. And, Tokyo-based Rating and Investment Information now says there is a "50% to 100%" chance that it will strip Japan of its top-notch rating before 2011 is out.\par \par \uc2 Despite all that, as well as a report from the International Monetary Fund that the country's fiscal position may be unsustainable, there is still no sign of some wholesale reversal of investment flows.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, the latest flows data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that foreign investors bought Y737.4 billion of short-dated securities in the week to last Friday. This was the fourth week of such inflows, which totalled the equivalent of about $29 billion.\par \par \uc2 Sure, Japanese investors have also been investing abroad in their continued search for better returns than are available at home.\par \par \uc2 But, the safe-haven flows that have been supporting the yen for months are only likely to intensify as the euro-zone debt crisis gets worse and the outlook for the global economy darkens.\par \par \uc2 Slower growth in China, fears of recession in the U.K. and the continued risk that the euro will implode is likely to keep global investors on their toes, searching for markets where they deem risk to be minimal.\par \par \uc2 For the moment, the yen remains just such a place.\par \par \uc2 Even though the return of deflation, with prices in Tokyo falling 0.8% this month and analysts looking for little recovery by 2013, and the risk of a downgrade should make Japan less attractive, the rise in global concerns means that the yen is unlikely to lose its allure.\par \par \uc2 Of course, recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has discouraged market participants from pushing the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too far or too fast.\par \par \uc2 And the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent decline probably has more to do with profit-taking than any reversal in sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Given that, the yen will more than likely bounce back, proving once again that it is about as invincible as The Terminator of Hollywood film fame.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg TNI FRX POV\par \par \uc2 Reuters USD/DJ\par \par \uc2 Thomson P/1066 or P/1074\par \par \uc2 (Nicholas Hastings is a Senior Correspondent in London for Dow Jones Newswires who has written about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than 20 years. He previously covered a variety of markets, including equities, fixed income, commodities and energy. He can be contacted on +44-20-7842-9493 or by email: nick.hastings@dowjones.com) [ 25-11-11 1128GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1066   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111125e7bp000pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
