\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 22\b0\par\par\uc2 1,721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2011\par 08:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RATINGS FIRMS REACT TO LATEST US BUDGET FAILURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The short statement came after a congressional committee tasked with slashing the U.S. budget gap failed to reach an agreement, a setback that triggers mandatory cuts to military spending and some social programs starting in 2013. (published 0114 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER WARY OF FOREIGN BOND-BUYING SCHEME TO WEAKEN YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister Tuesday shot down the idea of buying large amounts of foreign bonds to weaken the yen, saying it doesn't fit well with the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WORLD BANK: GROWTH IN EAST ASIA TO MODERATE DUE TO WEAKER EXTERNAL DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economic growth in East Asia continues to moderate, mainly due to weakening external demand, underscoring the need for governments to focus on driving local demand and productivity amid uncertainties in Europe and a global growth slowdown, the World Bank said in a report. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD BANK: CHINA SURPLUS WILL FALL IF REAL YUAN FURTHER APPRECIATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's current account surplus may continue to decline, especially if the yuan appreciates further in real terms, World Bank China Economist Ardo Hansson said Tuesday. (published 0409 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: FORMER PBOC ADVISER: CONTROLLING INFLATION NO LONGER A POLICY PRIORITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation has peaked and controlling price growth is no longer a policy priority, a former adviser to the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: DIFFICULT FOR ECONOMY TO GROW AT DOUBLE-DIGIT RATE GOING FORWARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It will be difficult for China's economy to grow at a double-digit rate going forward as exports will face increased pressure next year due to weakening U.S. and European economies, an adviser to the People's Bank of China said Tuesday. (published 0706 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS GLOBAL ECON CONDITIONS VERY DIFFICULT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's government plans to issue its mid year budget review by the end of the calendar year and it will be framed against a backdrop of "very difficult global economic conditions," Treasurer Wayne Swan said Tuesday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JPMORGAN SAYS AUSTRALIA'S RBA TO CUT RATES 25 BPS IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will cut interest rates in the country to 4.25% from the current 4.50% when the bank meets in December, \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA GOVT ECONOMIST: ECONOMIC GROWTH WILL SLOW TO 'MEDIUM' SPEED NEXT FEW YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic growth will likely slow to "medium" speed--that is, growth of 6%-7% annually--over the next few years, with a slowdown in investment growth, a government economist said at a forum Tuesday. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD BANK: CHINA COULD STILL SEE SOFT LANDING ON POLICY ADJUSTMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China faces rising risks to its economic growth from areas such as its weakening property market, but ample room for policy adjustment means Beijing should still be able to guide the economy toward a moderate slowdown, the World Bank said in a report Tuesday. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC, HKMA DOUBLE SIZE OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -SWAP DEAL TO CNY400 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China and Hong Kong said Tuesday they have doubled the value of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap to CNY400 billion as Beijing seeks to expand the pool of yuan traded offshore. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA SHORT-TERM DEBT FALLS BY THE MOST SINCE 2008 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's short-term external debt declined in the third quarter by the most since the fourth quarter of 2008, during the global financial crisis, due to the repatriation of funds by foreign banks, while the government's efforts to reduce the risk of sudden rapid capital outflows are also taking effect. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIAN RUPEE FALLS TO NEW ALL-TIME LOW AGAINST US DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian rupee tumbled to a new all-time low against the U.S. dollar Tuesday as importers continued to accumulate the greenback on fears that the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would weaken further in the absence of any aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FINANCE MINISTER: RUPEE'S WEAKNESS DUE TO GLOBAL UNCERTAINTIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  has limited scope to check the rupee's decline against the dollar as the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness stems from global uncertainties that are driving investors to the safe-haven greenback, the finance minister said Tuesday. (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN REGULATOR ASKS LOCAL BANKS TO RAISE LOAN-LOSS PROVISIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's financial regulator on Tuesday asked domestic banks to increase their loan-loss provisions to strengthen the island's banking system, as the worsening global economic outlook is increasing the risk of loan defaults. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: NEW \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STRATEGY LEAVES MARKETS UNCERTAIN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's new tactics for trying to weaken the yen, mixing highly public forays into the market with stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has left market players uncertain over what may come next, which appears to be just what the authorities want. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: SINGAPORE OCTOBER CPI LIKELY ROSE 5.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's consumer price inflation likely edged lower in October, as previous rounds of tightening by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a slowing global economy begun to bite. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: HURDLES AHEAD AS TOKYO, OSAKA EXCHANGES AGREE ON MERGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Tokyo and Osaka stock exchanges said Tuesday that they aim to merge in January 2013 as grim market performance and a global wave of consolidation compel them to unite. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: US AGENCY SIDES AGAINST HTC IN PATENT CASE VS APPLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. International Trade Commission ruled that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . products don't infringe on patents held by \f28 \uc2 \f2 HTC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s recently acquired subsidiary S3 Graphics, a setback for the Android handset maker. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NANYA TECHNOLOGY FILES PATENT INFRINGEMENT COMPLAINT AGAINST ELPIDA, KINGSTON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nanya Technology Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . filed Tuesday a patent infringement complaint against Japanese chip rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Elpida Memory Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., its U.S. unit and California-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kingston Technology Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . after a similar action from Elpida last week against the Taiwanese memory chipmaker. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CENTRO INVESTORS BACK RESTRUCTURE TO STAY AFLOAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Centro Properties Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is set to avoid liquidation after investors approved a restructure plan. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HAIRUN MEDIA GETS HK REGULATORY OK FOR UP TO US$200 MLN HK IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing-based Hairun Media & Entertainment Group Ltd. received Hong Kong regulatory approval Monday for its plan to raise between US$150 million and US$200 million in an initial public offering ahead of a mid-December listing, a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OIL & NATURAL GAS CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  WITHDRAWS SHARE SALE PROSPECTUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oil & Natural Gas Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday said it has shelved its proposed follow-on share sale. (published 0314 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OLYMPUS FORMER CEO WOODFORD TO MEET OLYMPUS BOARD IN JAPAN ON FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Olympus Corp. Chief Executive Michael Woodford will meet with the board of directors that fired him on Friday, during his first trip to Japan since he was ousted from his post in mid-October. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN GOVERNMENT TIGHTENS DAILY CAP OF STOCKS SHORT-SELLING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's government said Tuesday it tightened the daily limit of stocks short-selling in a bid to stabilize the local equity market as the euro-zone debt crisis persists. (published 2355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NEW CHINA LIFE TO START A-SHARE IPO ROADSHOW WEDNESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New China Life Insurance Co. set the stage for a December float in Shanghai and Hong Kong as it will start to meet investors Wednesday for the mainland portion of the dual listing. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : TO PROVIDE SUZUKI WITH COMMERCIAL ELECTRIC MINI VEHICLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it will expand its production tie-up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Suzuki Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to include the supply of small commercial electric vans. (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : PLAN TO UNVEIL GOOGLE TV NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's largest flat-screen television maker by volume, said Tuesday it plans to unveil a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  TV next year, though not at the Consumer Electronics Show in January. (published 0245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JET AIRWAYS\f28 \uc2 \f2  AUDITORS ASK COMPANY TO RAISE FUNDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jet Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s auditors have asked the company, the country's largest carrier by market share, to raise fresh capital to meet its obligations and fund loss-making unit JetLite. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par XSTRATA: REVIEWING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AFTER ORICA PLANT SHUTDOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Top coal exporter \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is reviewing all its mine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Australia's New South Wales state after a shutdown at an explosives plant run by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Orica Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . that could pressure miners in one of the world's largest coal export basins, a spokesman said Tuesday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S GRYPHON MINERALS CUTS CAPITAL RAISING PRICE - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gryphon Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has lowered the price of its proposed A$63 million capital raising due to a lack of demand, according to person familiar with the matter. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COSCO GROUP: INTERESTED IN INVESTING IN US PORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Ocean Shipping Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chairman Wei Jiafu said Tuesday the group is interested in investing in ports in the U.S., amid the global shipping industry downturn. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: XSTRATA CONCERNED WITH LATEST DRAFT OF AUSTRALIA MINING TAX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's largest coal exporter, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,, has concerns with some parts of a draft mining tax law due to pass Australia's parliament as soon as tonight and will lobby Canberra to remove any changes, the company's global coal chief said Tuesday. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KYUSHU ELECTRIC GETS Y60B JBIC LOAN FOR LNG PURCHASES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 22-11-11 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japan Bank For International Cooperation Tuesday signed a deal to lend Y60 billion to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kyushu Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA OCTOBER COAL OUTPUT 330 MLN TONS, UP 7.3% ON YEAR -ASSOCIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China produced 330 million metric tons of coal in October, an increase of 7.3% from a year earlier, data from the China Coal Transportation and Distribution Association showed. (published 0412 GMT) [ 22-11-11 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111122e7bm000bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
