\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 954 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2011\par 13:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EURO-ZONE EXPORTS GROWTH LIFT TRADE INTO SURPLUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's balance in trade in goods with the rest of the world pushed into surplus in September as exports grew, at a time when other parts of the euro-zone economy are doing less well amid the deepening sovereign debt crisis, data from the European Union's statistics agency showed Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EURO-ZONE ECONOMY MAINTAINED MODEST EXPANSION IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro-zone economy continued to grow at a modest pace in the three months to the end of September, driven by pickups in consumer spending in Germany and France.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN 3Q GDP GREW IN LINE WITH EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)-German economic growth accelerated in the third quarter of this year in line with expectations, data from the Federal Statistics Office, Destatis, showed Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE'S KING: OUTLOOK FOR UK ECONOMY HAS WEAKENED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of England Governor Mervyn King said Tuesday the slowing global economy and euro-zone crisis are likely to have weakened the outlook for the U.K. economy and to have led to a greater and more persistent margin of spare capacity than previously thought.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN ECONOMIC EXPECTATIONS WORSEN MORE THAN FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German economic expectations deteriorated more than forecast in November as the government crises in Italy and Greece as well as the debt problems of the euro zone and the U.S. dampened business sentiment considerably, the Center for European Economic Research, also known as ZEW, said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK INFLATION RATE FALLS TO 5.0% IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rate of inflation in the U.K. slowed more than expected in October, official data showed Tuesday, as a supermarket price war helped offset higher household utility bills.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRENCH ECONOMY RETURNS TO GROWTH IN THIRD QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The French economy returned to growth in the third quarter after contracting in the second, data from national statistics agency Insee showed Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EURO-ZONE DEFAULT INSURANCE COSTS HIT RECORDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring Italian, Spanish, French and Belgian debt against default shot to fresh records Tuesday, as persistent concerns about the ability of governments to implement austerity measures amid the specter of recession kept investors looking for cover.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM NODA: WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF EXCESSIVE MOVES IN THE YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda issued warnings about the rebounding yen Tuesday, saying the government will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rises in a way that looks "excessive" to him.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: EXPECTS BOJ TO TAKE PROPER STEPS IN DEALING WITH YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister voiced hope Tuesday that the Bank of Japan would continue its efforts to tackle the yen's strength, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gradually regains ground lost after last month's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Tokyo authorities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRIAN 3Q GDP +0.3% VS 2Q, +2.6% ON YEAR-WIFO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 VIENNA (Dow Jones)--Austrian economic growth continued to slow in the third quarter after a significant slowdown in the second quarter, the country's main economic institute WIFO said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY SEPTEMBER FOREIGN TRADE DEFICIT HALVES ON EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROME (Dow Jones)--Italy's trade deficit narrowed in September as exports outpaced imports, especially to non-European Union countries, national statistics agency Istat said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TURKEY SEPT CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT $6.8B VERSUS $4B IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Turkey's current account deficit widened on the month in line with forecasts in September, underscoring investor nerves over the fast-growing economy's exposure to shocks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA RBA SAYS NEUTRAL POLICY BEST FOR SUSTAINED GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday its decision to cut interest rates at the start of the month reflected a desire for a more neutral monetary policy, but signaled that the effect of an ongoing mining boom still posed the risk of needing to have interest rates back at a more restrictive level\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DUTCH GDP DECLINES ON QUARTERLY BASIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AMSTERDAM (Dow Jones)--The Netherlands' gross domestic product declined in the third quarter compared with the previous one, according to first estimates, the national statistics agency CBS said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: IMF: CHINA BANKING SYSTEM NEEDS TO RELY MORE ON MARKET MECHANISMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China needs to revamp its banking system so that it relies more on market mechanisms, such as interest rates, to head off a "steady build-up of financial sector vulnerabilities," the International Monetary Fund said, in its first broad review of China's financial system.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO SPEED UP 1H 2012 SPENDING AMID GROWTH WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan said Tuesday the government will likely speed up budget spending in the first half of 2012, because it expects tougher growth conditions during that period than in the second half, highlighting increasing concerns about slowing growth momentum in Asia's fourth-largest economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: ASIAN COUNTRIES NEED CURBS TO COUNTERACT SPECULATIVE CAPITAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Tuesday said regulatory measures to curb the negative impact of rapid capital flows is crucial for Asian economies to counteract speculation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EU TO SET OUT LEGISLATION TO CURB RATING AGENCIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe Tuesday sets out long-awaited proposals to regulate credit rating agencies whose assessments are considered to have played a key role in the sovereign debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: STERLING SHOULD SHINE ON THROUGH NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sterling has just become a better bet. First, inflationary crosswinds that threatened to throw the U.K. economy entirely off course are finally dying down. And second, deteriorating support for the euro, despite all the political efforts to resolve the debt crisis, suggests that investor interest in the pound--and gilts--will only grow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-11-11 1201GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111115e7bf000vu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngbli