erest rates, to head off a "steady build-up of financial sector vulnerabilities," the International Monetary Fund said, in its first broad review of China's financial system.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO SPEED UP 1H 2012 SPENDING AMID GROWTH WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan said Tuesday the government will likely speed up budget spending in the first half of 2012, because it expects tougher growth conditions during that period than in the second half, highlighting increasing concerns about slowing growth momentum in Asia's fourth-largest economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: ASIAN COUNTRIES NEED CURBS TO COUNTERACT SPECULATIVE CAPITAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Tuesday said regulatory measures to curb the negative impact of rapid capital flows is crucial for Asian economies to counteract speculation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EU TO SET OUT LEGISLATION TO CURB RATING AGENCIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe Tuesday sets out long-awaited proposals to regulate credit rating agencies whose assessments are considered to have played a key role in the sovereign debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-11-11 1058GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111115e7bf000tr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
