\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options:Euro/Yen Options Fall Amid Eased European Tension\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2011\par 04:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Euro/yen options fell Monday in Asia as concerns over the European sovereign debt crisis appeared to have eased for now on expectations that new leaders in Italy and Greece will swiftly undertake necessary fiscal reforms.\par \par \uc2 As of 0200 GMT, benchmark volatilities implied by one-month at-the-money euro/yen options were at 15.45%/16.55% from 16.63%/17.37% Friday in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Italian new Prime Minister Mario Monti over the weekend said he would name his new cabinet "with urgency" addressing the need to appease markets quickly.\par \par \uc2 Greece named former European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Lucas Papademos as its next prime minister late last week.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, volatilities implied by one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options were steady at 9.35%/9.65%, compared with 8.98%/9.62% Friday in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "Some are talking about the potential for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and what not, but that's nothing compared to what is going on in Europe," said an options dealer at a major Japanese trust bank.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 1 Month Option Implied Volatilities At 0200 GMT \par  \par              Tokyo          New York       Tokyo \par              Monday         Friday         Friday \par Dollar/Yen   9.35%/9.65%    Market closed  8.98%/9.62% \par Euro/Dollar  14.85%/15.25%                 15.95%/16.35% \par Euro/Yen     15.45%/16.55%                 16.63%/17.37% \par  \par  \par 3 Month Option Implied Volatilities At 0200 GMT \par  \par              Tokyo          Tokyo \par              Monday         Friday \par Dollar/Yen   9.75%/10.15%   9.84%/10.24% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volatilities used are over-the-counter, at-the-money rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1-month 25 delta risk-reversals favor dollar put/yen call options by -0.20%/0.70% compared with -0.05%/0.55% in Tokyo on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Kosaku Narioka, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2784; kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com [ 14-11-11 0336GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1077 4127   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111114e7be0006g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
