ectronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  tacked on 1.6% in Seoul. Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woodside Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 1.8% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Origin Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  added 1.5%, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  advanced 1.4%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was roughly steady against the U.S. dollar as investors remained circumspect about the sovereign-debt situation in Europe despite the appointment of a new leader in Italy over the weekend and in Greece last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Markets are likely to be cautious in their enthusiasm for the new governments at this stage. Both have a fragile hold on political power and their capacity to implement the kinds of reform needed to restore market confidence is yet to be tested," said Ric Spooner Chief Markets Analyst at CMC Markets\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at $1.3768 against the dollar, from $1.3755 late Monday in New York, and at Y106.12 against the yen, from Y106.40. The dollar was at Y77.16, from Y77.14.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold was at $1,790.90 per troy ounce, up $2.40 from its New York settlement on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December Nymex crude oil futures were up six cents at $99.05 per barrel on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES \par Monti Asked To Form Government, Says Italy Can Overcome Crisis \par Obama Pressures China's Hu On \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Rebalancing \par China's Hu: Even Big Rise In Yuan Can't Resolve U.S Problems - Xinhua \par Obama, Leaders Announce Outlines Of Trans-Pacific Trade Pact \par Berlusconi's Party To Support 'Technical' Monti Govt \par ECB Weidmann: ECB Not Lender Of Last Resort For Governments -FT \par France,Germany To New Greek Prime Minister:Must Honor Commitments \par China To US: Yuan Is At 'Fair-Value'--Xinhua \par ECB Orphanides: Greek Debt Write-down Harmful To Euro Zone-Paper \par German Govt Prepares For Greece To Exit Euro \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Union - Report \par China Urges More Trade With Southeast-Asian Nations \par Japan's Free-Trade Move Criticized \par Swiss Economy Minister Warns Against Pushing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  To Weaken Franc \par Greeks Welcome Papademos, Coalition Government - Polls \par Japan, China Agree To Join Forces On Global Financial Challenges \par Malaysian PM Najib: Won't Invest In European Rescue \par INTERVIEW: Thai Deputy PM: Determined To Stay As Southeast Asia's Industrial Hub \par IBM, Chinese Company Suning Appliance In E-Commerce Pact \par Singapore Prime Minister: Growth Likely Slow Over Next Few Quarters \par WSJ UPDATE: IMF Head Suggests \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Justified \par Singapore Sovereign Fund Sold Most Of Olympus Stake \par Libya NOC Head Sees Oil Output At Pre-War Level By End '12 \par Arab League Suspends Syria, Effective Wed \par NZ 3Q Real Retail Sales +2.2% Vs 2Q; Consensus +0.6% \par Greece Names New Cabinet \par Obama Warns Budget Supercommittee, Urges Action \par SEC Employees Disciplined Over Madoff Case \par S&P Says Computer Glitch Led To Erroneous Message \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sale Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 EMI Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Nears Conclusion \par Reuters/Univ Michigan Mid-Nov Sentiment Climbs \par More Than 1,000 \f28 \uc2 \f2 MF Global\f28 \uc2 \f2  Staff Fired \par Mexican Interior Minister Killed In Crash \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 11-13-11 2203ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62500   \par \par \uc2 Dokument NRG0000020111114e7be0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley